{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 22:43:05", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-d66b96b7-2111-4437-a2a6-7eb165f48a38', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/design-phase-pause-fix/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Design Phase Pause Fix Implementation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01FkoU7Hwk5ha7VrVcJ6kXNy', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/design-phase-pause-fix/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01FkoU7Hwk5ha7VrVcJ6kXNy', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Requirements: Design Phase Pause Fix Implementation\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n**Project Name**: Design Phase Pause Fix Implementation\\n**Purpose**: Fix the agent pipeline termination issue when agents return `needs_user_input` status during the design phase\\n**Priority**: High - critical bug fix\\n**TDD Required**: Yes - write tests first, then implementation\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\nCurrently, when an Executive Director agent returns `status: \\"needs_user_input\\"` during the design phase, the backend incorrectly marks the agent as \\"completed\\" instead of pausing execution to wait for user input. This causes the pipeline to terminate prematurely, preventing proper user interaction and continuation.\\n\\n## Core Requirements\\n\\n### 1. Agent Status Handling (CRITICAL)\\n- **REQ-001**: `_execute_agent_background` method MUST detect `needs_user_input` status from agent results\\n- **REQ-002**: Agents with `needs_user_input` status MUST be marked as `\\"awaiting_user_input\\"` (NOT \\"completed\\")\\n- **REQ-003**: Agent context MUST be preserved for later continuation including:\\n  - Original input data\\n  - Question asked to user\\n  - Agent type information\\n- **REQ-004**: Agent logs MUST reflect waiting state with appropriate message\\n\\n### 2. Question-Answer Flow (CRITICAL)\\n- **REQ-005**: `answer_question` endpoint MUST trigger agent continuation after recording answer\\n- **REQ-006**: System MUST match answers to waiting agents using question_id\\n- **REQ-007**: Answer processing MUST happen asynchronously to avoid blocking response\\n\\n### 3. Agent Continuation (CRITICAL) \\n- **REQ-008**: New `continue_agent_with_answer` method MUST spawn fresh agent with continuation context\\n- **REQ-009**: Continuation context MUST include:\\n  - Original task input\\n  - Previous question\\n  - User\'s answer\\n  - Clear instruction to continue implementation\\n- **REQ-010**: Agent continuation MUST use Executive Director agent type for consistency\\n\\n### 4. Data Structure Requirements\\n- **REQ-011**: `active_agents[agent_id]` MUST support new fields:\\n  - `awaiting_question_id`: Links agent to pending question\\n  - `continuation_context`: Stores resumption data\\n- **REQ-012**: Status field MUST support `\\"awaiting_user_input\\"` state\\n- **REQ-013**: State transitions MUST follow: `running \\u2192 awaiting_user_input \\u2192 [answer] \\u2192 running \\u2192 completed`\\n\\n## Implementation Scope\\n\\n### Files to Modify\\n- **Primary**: `backend/main.py` - All core changes\\n- **Secondary**: Test files for validation\\n\\n### Components to Change\\n1. **`_execute_agent_background` method** (modify existing)\\n2. **`answer_question` endpoint** (modify existing) \\n3. **`continue_agent_with_answer` method** (add new)\\n\\n## Testing Requirements (TDD)\\n\\n### Unit Tests (MUST IMPLEMENT)\\n- **TEST-001**: Verify `_execute_agent_background` correctly detects `needs_user_input`\\n- **TEST-002**: Verify continuation context is properly stored and structured\\n- **TEST-003**: Verify `continue_agent_with_answer` builds correct input data\\n- **TEST-004**: Verify state transitions work correctly\\n- **TEST-005**: Verify question_id matching logic works\\n\\n### Integration Tests (MUST IMPLEMENT)\\n- **TEST-006**: Mock agent returns `needs_user_input` \\u2192 verify status becomes `awaiting_user_input`\\n- **TEST-007**: Submit answer \\u2192 verify new agent spawned with correct context\\n- **TEST-008**: End-to-end flow from question through continuation to completion\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n- \\u2705 Agent pipeline NO LONGER terminates when `needs_user_input` is returned\\n- \\u2705 User sees appropriate \\"waiting\\" status in UI\\n- \\u2705 User can provide answer and agent continues with full context\\n- \\u2705 All tests pass (unit + integration)\\n- \\u2705 No regression in normal (non-question) agent execution flow\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Persistent storage for paused agents (agents lost on server restart)\\n- Multiple question support (one question per agent session)\\n- Question timeout handling\\n- Hot reload of agent definitions during continuation\\n- UI changes (backend focus only)\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- **Language**: Python (FastAPI backend)\\n- **Testing Framework**: pytest\\n- **Async**: Must use async/await patterns for continuations\\n- **Backwards Compatibility**: Must not break existing agent execution\\n- **Error Handling**: Must gracefully handle missing agents or invalid question_ids\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Question tracking system already exists and works correctly\\n- Executive Director agent can handle continuation context appropriately\\n- UI will properly display `awaiting_user_input` status\\n- Single concurrent answer per question_id (no race conditions expected)\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- Existing `AgentOrchestrator` class\\n- Existing question tracking system\\n- FastAPI BackgroundTasks for async processing\\n- Current agent spawning infrastructure"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01G2hVqFpQR1KH1xzqaBRFWy', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Design Phase Pause Fix Implementation', 'description': 'Fix agent pipeline termination issue when agents return needs_user_input status during the design phase'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01G2hVqFpQR1KH1xzqaBRFWy', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "681b869c", "message": "Created project: Design Phase Pause Fix Implementation", "summary": {"project_id": "681b869c", "project_name": "Design Phase Pause Fix Implementation", "description": "Fix agent pipeline termination issue when agents return needs_user_input status during the design phase", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T22:43:00.560644", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T22:43:00.560644", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T22:43:00.560644", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Design Phase Pause Fix Implementation\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01P9ckehs2udy2rxH7UjYUwe', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/design-phase-pause-fix/requirements.md', 'project_name': 'Design Phase Pause Fix Implementation'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01P9ckehs2udy2rxH7UjYUwe', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Missing required input field: output_file"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 79.8%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.8\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError, CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError, CircuitBreakerOpenError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I successfully executed the complete Development Manager workflow for this simple but well-structured project. I effectively managed the sequential process: milestone planning, architecture coordinati...\n- I effectively executed the complete planning and implementation workflow for Milestone 1. Successfully coordinated with System Architect for architecture design, spawned all three Coordinators for com...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create