{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 22:43:12", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-9b12b554-4932-4857-b361-4e54fa8fdb48', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/design-phase-pause-fix/requirements.md",\n  "project_name": "Design Phase Pause Fix Implementation",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01SHfL3ghbWvxiVAydUWbDEF', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/design-phase-pause-fix/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01SHfL3ghbWvxiVAydUWbDEF', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Requirements: Design Phase Pause Fix Implementation\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n**Project Name**: Design Phase Pause Fix Implementation\\n**Purpose**: Fix the agent pipeline termination issue when agents return `needs_user_input` status during the design phase\\n**Priority**: High - critical bug fix\\n**TDD Required**: Yes - write tests first, then implementation\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\nCurrently, when an Executive Director agent returns `status: \\"needs_user_input\\"` during the design phase, the backend incorrectly marks the agent as \\"completed\\" instead of pausing execution to wait for user input. This causes the pipeline to terminate prematurely, preventing proper user interaction and continuation.\\n\\n## Core Requirements\\n\\n### 1. Agent Status Handling (CRITICAL)\\n- **REQ-001**: `_execute_agent_background` method MUST detect `needs_user_input` status from agent results\\n- **REQ-002**: Agents with `needs_user_input` status MUST be marked as `\\"awaiting_user_input\\"` (NOT \\"completed\\")\\n- **REQ-003**: Agent context MUST be preserved for later continuation including:\\n  - Original input data\\n  - Question asked to user\\n  - Agent type information\\n- **REQ-004**: Agent logs MUST reflect waiting state with appropriate message\\n\\n### 2. Question-Answer Flow (CRITICAL)\\n- **REQ-005**: `answer_question` endpoint MUST trigger agent continuation after recording answer\\n- **REQ-006**: System MUST match answers to waiting agents using question_id\\n- **REQ-007**: Answer processing MUST happen asynchronously to avoid blocking response\\n\\n### 3. Agent Continuation (CRITICAL) \\n- **REQ-008**: New `continue_agent_with_answer` method MUST spawn fresh agent with continuation context\\n- **REQ-009**: Continuation context MUST include:\\n  - Original task input\\n  - Previous question\\n  - User\'s answer\\n  - Clear instruction to continue implementation\\n- **REQ-010**: Agent continuation MUST use Executive Director agent type for consistency\\n\\n### 4. Data Structure Requirements\\n- **REQ-011**: `active_agents[agent_id]` MUST support new fields:\\n  - `awaiting_question_id`: Links agent to pending question\\n  - `continuation_context`: Stores resumption data\\n- **REQ-012**: Status field MUST support `\\"awaiting_user_input\\"` state\\n- **REQ-013**: State transitions MUST follow: `running \\u2192 awaiting_user_input \\u2192 [answer] \\u2192 running \\u2192 completed`\\n\\n## Implementation Scope\\n\\n### Files to Modify\\n- **Primary**: `backend/main.py` - All core changes\\n- **Secondary**: Test files for validation\\n\\n### Components to Change\\n1. **`_execute_agent_background` method** (modify existing)\\n2. **`answer_question` endpoint** (modify existing) \\n3. **`continue_agent_with_answer` method** (add new)\\n\\n## Testing Requirements (TDD)\\n\\n### Unit Tests (MUST IMPLEMENT)\\n- **TEST-001**: Verify `_execute_agent_background` correctly detects `needs_user_input`\\n- **TEST-002**: Verify continuation context is properly stored and structured\\n- **TEST-003**: Verify `continue_agent_with_answer` builds correct input data\\n- **TEST-004**: Verify state transitions work correctly\\n- **TEST-005**: Verify question_id matching logic works\\n\\n### Integration Tests (MUST IMPLEMENT)\\n- **TEST-006**: Mock agent returns `needs_user_input` \\u2192 verify status becomes `awaiting_user_input`\\n- **TEST-007**: Submit answer \\u2192 verify new agent spawned with correct context\\n- **TEST-008**: End-to-end flow from question through continuation to completion\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n- \\u2705 Agent pipeline NO LONGER terminates when `needs_user_input` is returned\\n- \\u2705 User sees appropriate \\"waiting\\" status in UI\\n- \\u2705 User can provide answer and agent continues with full context\\n- \\u2705 All tests pass (unit + integration)\\n- \\u2705 No regression in normal (non-question) agent execution flow\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Persistent storage for paused agents (agents lost on server restart)\\n- Multiple question support (one question per agent session)\\n- Question timeout handling\\n- Hot reload of agent definitions during continuation\\n- UI changes (backend focus only)\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- **Language**: Python (FastAPI backend)\\n- **Testing Framework**: pytest\\n- **Async**: Must use async/await patterns for continuations\\n- **Backwards Compatibility**: Must not break existing agent execution\\n- **Error Handling**: Must gracefully handle missing agents or invalid question_ids\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Question tracking system already exists and works correctly\\n- Executive Director agent can handle continuation context appropriately\\n- UI will properly display `awaiting_user_input` status\\n- Single concurrent answer per question_id (no race conditions expected)\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- Existing `AgentOrchestrator` class\\n- Existing question tracking system\\n- FastAPI BackgroundTasks for async processing\\n- Current agent spawning infrastructure"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 96.7%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.5\n- Common errors to avoid: RateLimitError, CircuitBreakerOpenError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: RateLimitError, CircuitBreakerOpenError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- The architecture successfully addresses the experimental validation requirements by providing a scientifically rigorous framework for comparing AI models in TDD scenarios. The modular design enables c...\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the simple requirement while establishing maintainable patterns for potential future enhancements. The approach balances the minimal scope with profess...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['tod