{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 22:43:18", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-1f11e53d-ffe3-4a57-aac6-6561b39ce8c2', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Agent Families Implementation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01LNoPx5L6nBMRWisvSG8D6z', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01LNoPx5L6nBMRWisvSG8D6z', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Agent Families Implementation Requirements\\n\\n## Project Vision\\nImplement a family-based naming and achievement system for agent groups to provide visual cohesion and collective tracking across the ensemble. This system will enhance user understanding of agent relationships and provide engaging gamification elements.\\n\\n## Core Objectives\\n\\n### Primary Objective\\nCreate a cohesive family system that automatically assigns memorable names to related agent groups and tracks collective achievements to enhance user experience and provide insight into agent collaboration patterns.\\n\\n### Success Criteria\\n1. **Family Naming**: All new agent tasks spawn with unique, whimsical family names that are inherited by child agents\\n2. **Achievement Tracking**: Family-level achievements are tracked and displayed, including task completion, efficiency, and collaboration metrics\\n3. **Visual Integration**: Family information is seamlessly integrated into the existing UI with clear visual groupings and achievement displays\\n4. **Performance**: System adds minimal overhead (< 5ms per operation) to existing agent workflows\\n5. **Test Coverage**: 90%+ test coverage on all new functionality using TDD methodology\\n\\n## Detailed Requirements\\n\\n### 1. Family Name Generation System\\n**Core Functionality**:\\n- Generate whimsical, memorable family names using adjective + noun pattern\\n- Ensure name uniqueness using hash + timestamp methodology\\n- Store family names in agent metadata and runtime state\\n- Provide < 1ms generation time per name\\n\\n**Technical Requirements**:\\n- Implement `name_generator.py` with curated word lists\\n- Update `runtime.py` for family name assignment on agent spawn\\n- Ensure backwards compatibility (family name field optional for legacy agents)\\n- Include comprehensive unit tests\\n\\n### 2. Family Inheritance Mechanism\\n**Core Functionality**:\\n- Child agents automatically inherit parent\'s family name\\n- Maintain family relationships across agent hierarchies\\n- Support family lineage tracking for debugging and analysis\\n\\n**Technical Requirements**:\\n- Modify agent spawning logic to propagate family names\\n- Ensure inheritance works across all agent types\\n- Maintain referential integrity in family relationships\\n\\n### 3. Activity Tracker & Achievement System\\n**Core Functionality**:\\n- Aggregate family-level metrics from individual agent activities\\n- Track at least 3 achievement types:\\n  - **Collective Task Completion**: Family completes X tasks\\n  - **Efficiency Badge**: Family achieves under time/iteration targets  \\n  - **Collaboration Star**: Family members assist each other\\n- Persist achievements with queryable interface\\n\\n**Technical Requirements**:\\n- Update `activity_tracker.py` with family-level aggregation\\n- Implement achievement definitions and tracking logic\\n- Ensure performance overhead < 5ms per tracking operation\\n- Include comprehensive unit tests for achievement logic\\n\\n### 4. API Integration\\n**Core Functionality**:\\n- Expose family information through REST endpoints\\n- Support family data retrieval and achievement queries\\n- Follow existing API patterns for consistency\\n\\n**Technical Requirements**:\\n- Implement API endpoints for family information\\n- Ensure proper error handling and validation\\n- Maintain API versioning compatibility\\n\\n### 5. Frontend Integration\\n**Core Functionality**:\\n- Display family names in all agent displays\\n- Provide visual grouping of family members in hierarchy view\\n- Show achievement badges for families\\n- Update UI components to show family relationships\\n\\n**Technical Requirements**:\\n- Update React components following existing UI patterns\\n- Ensure responsive design and accessibility\\n- Implement visual indicators for family-based relationships\\n- Include end-to-end integration tests\\n\\n## Technical Stack & Constraints\\n\\n### Technology Decisions\\n- **Backend**: Python with existing FastAPI framework\\n- **Frontend**: React with existing component patterns\\n- **Storage**: Extend existing agent metadata structure\\n- **Name Generation**: Curated word lists with adjective + noun combinations\\n- **Testing**: TDD methodology with pytest and React Testing Library\\n\\n### Performance Constraints\\n- Name generation: < 1ms per operation\\n- Activity tracking: < 5ms overhead per operation\\n- API response times: Maintain existing performance standards\\n\\n### Compatibility Requirements\\n- Backwards compatibility with existing agents\\n- No breaking changes to current API contracts\\n- Graceful degradation for legacy agent data\\n\\n## Scope & Exclusions\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- Family name generation and inheritance\\n- Achievement tracking system (3 initial achievement types)\\n- API and frontend integration\\n- Comprehensive testing suite\\n- Performance optimization\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Advanced achievement types beyond the initial 3\\n- Family management UI (creation, editing, deletion)\\n- Historical achievement analytics\\n- Achievement rewards or gamification mechanics beyond badges\\n- Multi-project family tracking\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n1. **Performance Risk**: Profile all components to ensure performance targets are met\\n2. **Name Collision Risk**: Use hash + timestamp to guarantee uniqueness\\n3. **Backwards Compatibility Risk**: Make all family fields optional and provide defaults\\n4. **Integration Risk**: Implement comprehensive integration tests\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\nFollow TDD methodology:\\n1. Write tests first for each component\\n2. Implement minimal code to pass tests\\n3. Refactor for optimization and maintainability\\n4. Ensure 90%+ test coverage\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n- Existing agent metadata structure can be extended without breaking changes\\n- Current API framework supports new endpoint additions\\n- React frontend can accommodate new UI components\\n- Performance targets are achievable with current infrastructure\\n- Three achievement types provide sufficient initial value\\n\\n## Milestone Structure\\nImplementation will follow a three-milestone approach:\\n1. **M1**: Family name generation and inheritance core\\n2. **M2**: Activity tracker and family achievements  \\n3. **M3**: API and frontend integration\\n\\nEach milestone includes comprehensive testing and maintains backwards compatibility."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Ed1KNyNFxiNbiaccywpHJq', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Agent Families Implementation', 'description': 'Implement a family-based naming and achievement system for agent groups to enhance user understanding and collaboration tracking.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Ed1KNyNFxiNbiaccywpHJq', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "4b999fa2", "message": "Created project: Agent Families Implementation", "summary": {"project_id": "4b999fa2", "project_name": "Agent Families Implementation", "description": "Implement a family-based naming and achievement system for agent groups to enhance user understanding and collaboration tracking.", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T22:43:06.889387", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T22:43:06.889387", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T22:43:06.889387", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Agent Families Implementation\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Hnv6cZgmw9sVfKFGQSAwJj', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Agent Families Implementation Milestone Plan\n\n## Overall Project Goal\nImplement a family-based naming and achievement system for agent groups to provide visual cohesion and collective tracking across the ensemble.\n\n## Milestone Structure\n\n### Milestone 1: Family Name Generation Core\n**Objective**: Implement robust family name generation and inheritance mechanism\n**Deliverables**:\n- Family name generation system\n- Inheritance mechanism for agent hierarchies\n- Initial unit tests for name generation\n- Performance validation for name generation\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Generate unique, whimsical family names \n- Propagate family names across agent hierarchies\n- Name generation time < 1ms\n- 90%+ test coverage for name generation logic\n\n### Milestone 2: Activity Tracking & Achievements\n**Objective**: Create family-level activity tracking and achievement system\n**Deliverables**:\n- Activity aggregation mechanism\n- Three initial achievement types:\n  1. Collective Task Completion\n  2. Efficiency Badge\n  3. Collaboration Star\n- Persistence and query interface for achievements\n- Comprehensive unit tests\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Track family-level metrics\n- Implement 3 defined achievement types\n- Tracking operation overhead < 5ms\n- Queryable achievement interface\n- 90%+ test coverage for tracking logic\n\n### Milestone 3: API and Frontend Integration\n**Objective**: Seamlessly integrate family system into existing infrastructure\n**Deliverables**:\n- REST API endpoints for family information\n- Updated React components to display family relationships\n- Integration tests\n- Performance and compatibility validation\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Expose family data through REST endpoints\n- Update UI to show family names and achievements\n- Maintain existing performance standards\n- Backwards compatibility preserved\n- 90%+ test coverage for integration components\n\n## Cross-Cutting Requirements\n- Maintain < 5ms performance overhead\n- 90%+ test coverage across all components\n- No breaking changes to existing systems\n- Graceful handling of legacy agent data'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Hnv6cZgmw9sVfKFGQSAwJj', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_224318.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_224318.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 79.8%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.8\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError, CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError, CircuitBreakerOpenError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I successfully executed the complete Development Manager workflow for this simple but well-structured project. I effectively managed the sequential process: milestone planning, architecture coordinati...\n- I effectively executed the complete planning and implementation workflow for Milestone 1. Successfully coordinated with System Architect for architecture design, spawned all three Coordinators for com...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['