{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 22:43:31", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-03e15d71-d30b-4448-b099-9e05a8dc59a2', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/github-bots/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "GitHub Bots Implementation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01GZAwE9tLUgrRUQTuUKjUEW', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/github-bots/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01GZAwE9tLUgrRUQTuUKjUEW', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# GitHub Sync Bot Requirements\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n- **Milestone**: 2 of 6 in GitHub Bots Suite\\n- **Purpose**: Implement advanced git synchronization capabilities\\n\\n## Core Capabilities\\n1. Remote Synchronization\\n   - Fetch and pull operations from remote repositories\\n   - Support for multiple remote repositories\\n   \\n2. Branch Management\\n   - Rebase operations with robust conflict handling\\n   - Safe stash management (save, restore, list)\\n   \\n3. Error Handling\\n   - Detailed conflict detection\\n   - Clear error reporting\\n   - Preservation of uncommitted changes\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- \\u2713 Successfully rebase branch with upstream changes\\n- \\u2713 Safely stash uncommitted changes before sync\\n- \\u2713 Detect and report conflicts clearly\\n- \\u2713 Restore stashed changes after successful sync\\n- \\u2713 Complete operations within 30 seconds for typical repositories\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Use existing base classes and configuration system\\n- Implement using Test-Driven Development (TDD)\\n- Comprehensive error handling\\n- Logging of all synchronization events\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Full repository migration\\n- Complex merge conflict resolution\\n- Support for non-git version control systems\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Base git configuration and authentication are already set up\\n- Typical repository size is under 1GB\\n- Standard git workflow (single branch, linear history)"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01RMw2xVxr3sCCvTPBAApYjk', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# GitHub Sync Bot - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\n**Project**: GitHub Sync Bot Implementation\n**Type**: Milestone 2 of 6 in GitHub Bots Suite\n**Scope**: Advanced git synchronization capabilities\n\n## Milestone Breakdown\n\n### Milestone 1: Core Infrastructure & Remote Operations\n**Duration**: 3-4 days\n**Objective**: Establish foundational sync capabilities\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Remote repository connection management\n- Basic fetch/pull operations\n- Configuration system integration\n- Core error handling framework\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- ✓ Can connect to multiple remote repositories\n- ✓ Fetch operations complete successfully\n- ✓ Pull operations work without conflicts\n- ✓ Basic error logging implemented\n\n**Dependencies**: Base classes and configuration system\n\n### Milestone 2: Branch Management & Stash Operations\n**Duration**: 4-5 days\n**Objective**: Implement safe branch operations with stash management\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Stash save/restore/list functionality\n- Branch rebase capabilities\n- Uncommitted changes preservation\n- Enhanced conflict detection\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- ✓ Safely stash uncommitted changes before sync\n- ✓ Restore stashed changes after successful sync\n- ✓ Rebase operations work with conflict detection\n- ✓ Clear error reporting for conflicts\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 completion\n\n### Milestone 3: Advanced Error Handling & Performance\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\n**Objective**: Robust error handling and performance optimization\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Comprehensive conflict resolution reporting\n- Performance optimization for large repos\n- Complete logging system\n- Final testing and documentation\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- ✓ Operations complete within 30 seconds for typical repos\n- ✓ Detailed conflict detection and reporting\n- ✓ All synchronization events logged\n- ✓ Complete test coverage\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 2 completion\n\n## Success Metrics\n- All acceptance criteria met\n- Test coverage > 90%\n- Performance benchmarks achieved\n- Integration with existing bot suite\n- Documentation complete\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n- Use TDD to catch issues early\n- Incremental development approach\n- Regular integration testing\n- Clear rollback procedures for each milestone'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01RMw2xVxr3sCCvTPBAApYjk', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_224251.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_224251.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01GmqKxBxEaYWqSPAL9sPjDb', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/github-bots/requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'project_name': 'GitHub Sync Bot'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01GmqKxBxEaYWqSPAL9sPjDb', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Missing required input field: output_file"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01UmRxa8gbsnpZUvdDUUXrUZ', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/github-bots/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'GitHub Sync Bot'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01UmRxa8gbsnpZUvdDUUXrUZ', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": null}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01GfiUT7urbVKt6cGYTCAfi3', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01GfiUT7urbVKt6cGYTCAfi3', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# GitHub Sync Bot - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## A. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Purpose\\nA robust git synchronization bot designed to handle complex remote repository interactions with emphasis on safety, performance, and clear error reporting.\\n\\n### Architecture Pattern\\n- **Architectural Style**: Modular, Event-Driven Service\\n- **Core Design Pattern**: Command Pattern for git operations\\n- **Synchronization Model**: Asynchronous with comprehensive state management\\n\\n## B. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Languages and Frameworks\\n- **Primary Language**: Python 3.9+\\n- **Git Interaction**: GitPython library\\n- **Async Processing**: asyncio\\n- **Logging**: Structured logging with `loguru`\\n\\n### Rationale\\n- Python chosen for:\\n  - Strong typing\\n  - Excellent async support\\n  - Rich ecosystem for system automation\\n- GitPython provides low-level git operations with pythonic abstractions\\n- `asyncio` enables non-blocking synchronization processes\\n\\n## C. System Components\\n\\n1. **RepositorySyncManager**\\n   - Orchestrates entire synchronization workflow\\n   - Manages multiple repository interactions\\n   - Coordinates stash, rebase, and conflict detection\\n\\n2. **RemoteRepositoryHandler**\\n   - Handles remote repository connections\\n   - Manages fetch, pull operations\\n   - Supports multiple remote repository tracking\\n\\n3. **StashManager**\\n   - Safe stash creation and restoration\\n   - Tracks uncommitted changes\\n   - Provides rollback capabilities\\n\\n4. **ConflictResolver**\\n   - Detects synchronization conflicts\\n   - Generates detailed error reports\\n   - Preserves repository state during conflicts\\n\\n5. **EventLogger**\\n   - Comprehensive event logging\\n   - Structured log generation\\n   - Performance and error tracking\\n\\n## D. File/Directory Structure\\n```\\ngithub_sync_bot/\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 core/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 repository_sync_manager.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 remote_repository_handler.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 stash_manager.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 conflict_resolver.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 event_logger.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 configuration.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 main.py\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 tests/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 unit/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 integration/\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 logs/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 config.yaml\\n```\\n\\n## E. Data Model & State Management\\n\\n### Configuration\\n```yaml\\ngithub_sync_bot:\\n  timeout: 30  # seconds\\n  log_level: INFO\\n  repositories:\\n    - name: primary_repo\\n      url: https://github.com/example/repo\\n      branch: main\\n```\\n\\n### State Tracking\\n- Immutable state snapshots\\n- Comprehensive error state preservation\\n- Minimal in-memory state to ensure performance\\n\\n## F. API Design\\n\\n### Sync Operation Interface\\n```python\\nasync def synchronize_repository(\\n    repo_path: str, \\n    remote: str = \'origin\', \\n    branch: str = \'main\'\\n) -> SyncResult:\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\n    Synchronize a repository with specified parameters\\n    \\n    Returns:\\n    - Success/Failure status\\n    - Detailed operation log\\n    - Conflict information if applicable\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\n```\\n\\n## G. Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Runtime Environment\\n- Docker container for consistent deployment\\n- Kubernetes for scalable, managed execution\\n- CI/CD via GitHub Actions\\n\\n### Configuration Management\\n- Environment-based configuration\\n- Secrets management via secure vaults\\n\\n## H. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Testing Approach\\n- 100% Unit Test Coverage\\n- Integration Tests for Complex Workflows\\n- Mutation Testing for Robustness\\n\\n### Test Categories\\n1. Successful Synchronization Scenarios\\n2. Conflict Detection\\n3. Stash Management\\n4. Error Handling Paths\\n\\n## I. Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Alternative 1: Direct Git CLI Wrapper\\n- **Pros**: Lightweight, direct system interaction\\n- **Cons**: Less robust error handling, more complex scripting\\n\\n### Alternative 2: Full Git Server Implementation\\n- **Pros**: Complete control over synchronization\\n- **Cons**: Overengineered, significant complexity overhead\\n\\n## J. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n1. **Repository Size Limitations**\\n   - Mitigation: Implement chunked processing\\n   - Soft limit: 1GB (per requirement)\\n\\n2. **Authentication Failures**\\n   - Mitigation: Comprehensive credential management\\n   - Fallback to manual intervention\\n\\n3. **Network Instability**\\n   - Mitigation: Exponential backoff, reconnection strategies\\n\\n## K. Open Questions\\n\\n1. Specific authentication mechanism for multiple repositories\\n2. Detailed conflict resolution strategy beyond current scope\\n3. Performance tuning for large repositories\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThis architecture provides a robust, performant solution for git repository synchronization, meeting all specified requirements while maintaining flexibility for future enhancements."}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 79.8%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.8\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError, CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError, CircuitBreakerOpenError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I successfully executed the complete Development Manager workflow for this simple but well-structured project. I effectively managed the sequential process: milestone planning, architecture coordinati...\n- I effectively executed the complete planning and implementation workflow for Milestone 1. Successfully coordinated with System Architect for architecture design, spawned all three Coordinators for com...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
