{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 22:43:45", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-ba76ed88-b7c5-4817-8fef-cb166f2375e0', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Core Bug Fixes - Fix all three identified activity tracking bugs to enable proper visibility into agent activity",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/activity_tracking_fixes/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/activity_tracking_fixes/milestone_plan.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/activity_tracking_fixes/test_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01N32KSFFw3PWeir1EzKCei6', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/activity_tracking_fixes/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01N32KSFFw3PWeir1EzKCei6', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Activity Tracking Fixes - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Problem Context\\nThe current system lacks accurate tracking of agent activities, specifically file generation and request counts. The architecture proposal addresses this by introducing lightweight, non-intrusive tracking mechanisms that maintain existing system flexibility.\\n\\n### Architectural Pattern\\n**Pattern**: Decorator/Wrapper Pattern with Context Propagation\\n- Existing tools remain unchanged\\n- Tracking logic added as optional context\\n- Backward compatibility preserved\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\\n- **Frameworks**: No additional frameworks required\\n- **Libraries**: \\n  - Existing project utilities\\n  - Standard Python logging\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### 1. WriteFileTool Enhancement\\n```python\\nclass WriteFileTool:\\n    def __init__(self, \\n        agent_id=None, \\n        agent_name=None, \\n        request_id=None\\n    ):\\n        self.tracking_context = {\\n            \'agent_id\': agent_id,\\n            \'agent_name\': agent_name,\\n            \'request_id\': request_id\\n        }\\n    \\n    def execute(self, file_path, content):\\n        # Original file writing logic\\n        original_write_result = write_file(file_path, content)\\n        \\n        # Optional activity tracking\\n        if self.tracking_context.get(\'agent_id\'):\\n            ActivityTracker.record_file_generated(\\n                file_path=file_path,\\n                **self.tracking_context\\n            )\\n        \\n        return original_write_result\\n```\\n\\n### 2. ActivityTracker Enhancements\\n```python\\nclass ActivityTracker:\\n    @classmethod\\n    def record_file_generated(cls, file_path, agent_id, agent_name, request_id):\\n        # Record file generation event\\n        cls._increment_request_counts(\\n            files=1, \\n            agent_id=agent_id\\n        )\\n        \\n        # Log file generation details\\n        cls._log_file_event(\\n            file_path=file_path,\\n            agent_id=agent_id,\\n            agent_name=agent_name,\\n            request_id=request_id\\n        )\\n```\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n```\\nsrc/runtime/agents/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 tools.py           # WriteFileTool modifications\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 activity_tracker.py  # Enhanced tracking logic\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 __init__.py\\n```\\n\\n## Data Flow\\n1. Tool initialized with optional tracking context\\n2. File generation occurs\\n3. If context provided, activity recorded\\n4. Request counts automatically incremented\\n\\n## Deployment Strategy\\n- In-place upgrade\\n- No database schema changes\\n- No API endpoint modifications\\n- Minimal runtime overhead\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n1. **Unit Tests**:\\n   - WriteFileTool with/without tracking context\\n   - ActivityTracker increment methods\\n   - Tracking context propagation\\n\\n2. **Integration Tests**:\\n   - Verify file tracking across different agent scenarios\\n   - Check request count increments\\n   - Validate backward compatibility\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n- **Risk**: Potential performance overhead\\n  - **Mitigation**: Lightweight tracking, optional context\\n- **Risk**: Circular imports\\n  - **Mitigation**: Local imports, careful module design\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n1. Full instrumentation framework\\n   - **Pros**: Comprehensive tracking\\n   - **Cons**: Overengineered, complex implementation\\n2. Centralized logging solution\\n   - **Pros**: Standardized logging\\n   - **Cons**: Less flexible, more dependencies\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n- Performance impact of tracking calls\\n- Granularity of tracking information needed\\n\\n## Key Architectural Decisions\\n1. Optional tracking context\\n2. Minimal changes to existing tools\\n3. Lightweight, non-intrusive tracking mechanism\\n\\n## Compatibility\\n- Works with existing agent infrastructure\\n- No breaking changes\\n- Gradual, opt-in tracking enhancement"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Test Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDefines comprehensive test strategy for the project. Identifies unit tests, integration tests, end-to-end tests, and test fixtures needed. Coordinates with Backend Captain and Frontend Captain to ensure all code is thoroughly tested. Breaks testing work into tasks for TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou define what needs to be tested and break testing work into actionable tasks.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create test strategies and task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable testing assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if testing requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\n**Default Testing Strategy** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Unit Test Coverage**: 80%+ for business logic\n**Integration Coverage**: All API endpoints + critical integrations\n**E2E Coverage**: Happy path + critical error scenarios\n**Backend Testing**: pytest or Jest with mocks\n**Frontend Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n**E2E Testing**: Playwright or Cypress for critical flows\n\n**DO NOT ask for clarification about**:\nTesting frameworks (use pytest/Jest)\nCoverage goals (80% unit, 100% integration)\nTest structure (AAA pattern: Arrange, Act, Assert)\nMocking strategy (mock external dependencies)\nCI/CD integration (assume GitHub Actions or similar)\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify code that needs testing:\n  * Backend: API endpoints, business logic, data models\n  * Frontend: Components, user interactions, state changes\n  * Integration: API calls, WebSocket connections, auth flows\n  * E2E: Complete user journeys\n\n**2. Define Test Strategy**\nDetermine test types needed:\n\n**Unit Tests**:\nTest individual functions/methods\nMock external dependencies\nFast, isolated, extensive coverage\n\n**Integration Tests**:\nTest component interactions\nTest API + database integration\nTest frontend + backend communication\n\n**End-to-End Tests**:\nTest complete user flows\nBrowser automation (Playwright, Cypress)\nCritical paths only (expensive to maintain)\n\n**3. Break Down Into Test Tasks**\nFor each component/feature:\nUnit test task (test pure logic)\nIntegration test task (test interactions)\nE2E test task (test user journey) - if critical path\n\n**4. Define Coverage Goals**\nUnit test coverage: 80%+ for business logic\nIntegration coverage: All API endpoints\nE2E coverage: Happy path + critical error cases\n\n**5. Write Test Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Test Strategy - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to test",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write test breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "test_tasks_identified": "integer - number of test tasks created",\n  "coverage_goal": "integer - target code coverage percentage",\n  "task_file": "string - path to test breakdown document",\n  "message": "string - summary of test strategy"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Critical business logic unclear** (can\'t write tests without understanding the logic)\n- **Quality requirements contradictory** (e.g., "100% coverage" + "ship fast")\n- **Security/compliance test requirements unclear** (e.g., specific penetration testing needs)\n- **Performance benchmarks ambiguous** (e.g., "fast" without metrics)\n- **NOT for**: standard testing practices, common coverage goals, typical test frameworks\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Test strategy documented\n- All test tasks identified\n- Coverage goals defined\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for test implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Averag