{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 22:44:06", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-145cd790-2e42-437c-84f6-3e610525a41c', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Performance Benchmarking - Establish baseline performance metrics for current haiku model",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tdd_coordinator_model_validation_requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01JLKYdEtCKLnytE7sAnXAq2', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01JLKYdEtCKLnytE7sAnXAq2', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# GitHub Sync Bot - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## A. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Purpose\\nA robust git synchronization bot designed to handle complex remote repository interactions with emphasis on safety, performance, and clear error reporting.\\n\\n### Architecture Pattern\\n- **Architectural Style**: Modular, Event-Driven Service\\n- **Core Design Pattern**: Command Pattern for git operations\\n- **Synchronization Model**: Asynchronous with comprehensive state management\\n\\n## B. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Languages and Frameworks\\n- **Primary Language**: Python 3.9+\\n- **Git Interaction**: GitPython library\\n- **Async Processing**: asyncio\\n- **Logging**: Structured logging with `loguru`\\n\\n### Rationale\\n- Python chosen for:\\n  - Strong typing\\n  - Excellent async support\\n  - Rich ecosystem for system automation\\n- GitPython provides low-level git operations with pythonic abstractions\\n- `asyncio` enables non-blocking synchronization processes\\n\\n## C. System Components\\n\\n1. **RepositorySyncManager**\\n   - Orchestrates entire synchronization workflow\\n   - Manages multiple repository interactions\\n   - Coordinates stash, rebase, and conflict detection\\n\\n2. **RemoteRepositoryHandler**\\n   - Handles remote repository connections\\n   - Manages fetch, pull operations\\n   - Supports multiple remote repository tracking\\n\\n3. **StashManager**\\n   - Safe stash creation and restoration\\n   - Tracks uncommitted changes\\n   - Provides rollback capabilities\\n\\n4. **ConflictResolver**\\n   - Detects synchronization conflicts\\n   - Generates detailed error reports\\n   - Preserves repository state during conflicts\\n\\n5. **EventLogger**\\n   - Comprehensive event logging\\n   - Structured log generation\\n   - Performance and error tracking\\n\\n## D. File/Directory Structure\\n```\\ngithub_sync_bot/\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 core/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 repository_sync_manager.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 remote_repository_handler.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 stash_manager.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 conflict_resolver.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 event_logger.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 configuration.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 main.py\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 tests/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 unit/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 integration/\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 logs/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 config.yaml\\n```\\n\\n## E. Data Model & State Management\\n\\n### Configuration\\n```yaml\\ngithub_sync_bot:\\n  timeout: 30  # seconds\\n  log_level: INFO\\n  repositories:\\n    - name: primary_repo\\n      url: https://github.com/example/repo\\n      branch: main\\n```\\n\\n### State Tracking\\n- Immutable state snapshots\\n- Comprehensive error state preservation\\n- Minimal in-memory state to ensure performance\\n\\n## F. API Design\\n\\n### Sync Operation Interface\\n```python\\nasync def synchronize_repository(\\n    repo_path: str, \\n    remote: str = \'origin\', \\n    branch: str = \'main\'\\n) -> SyncResult:\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\n    Synchronize a repository with specified parameters\\n    \\n    Returns:\\n    - Success/Failure status\\n    - Detailed operation log\\n    - Conflict information if applicable\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\n```\\n\\n## G. Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Runtime Environment\\n- Docker container for consistent deployment\\n- Kubernetes for scalable, managed execution\\n- CI/CD via GitHub Actions\\n\\n### Configuration Management\\n- Environment-based configuration\\n- Secrets management via secure vaults\\n\\n## H. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Testing Approach\\n- 100% Unit Test Coverage\\n- Integration Tests for Complex Workflows\\n- Mutation Testing for Robustness\\n\\n### Test Categories\\n1. Successful Synchronization Scenarios\\n2. Conflict Detection\\n3. Stash Management\\n4. Error Handling Paths\\n\\n## I. Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Alternative 1: Direct Git CLI Wrapper\\n- **Pros**: Lightweight, direct system interaction\\n- **Cons**: Less robust error handling, more complex scripting\\n\\n### Alternative 2: Full Git Server Implementation\\n- **Pros**: Complete control over synchronization\\n- **Cons**: Overengineered, significant complexity overhead\\n\\n## J. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n1. **Repository Size Limitations**\\n   - Mitigation: Implement chunked processing\\n   - Soft limit: 1GB (per requirement)\\n\\n2. **Authentication Failures**\\n   - Mitigation: Comprehensive credential management\\n   - Fallback to manual intervention\\n\\n3. **Network Instability**\\n   - Mitigation: Exponential backoff, reconnection strategies\\n\\n## K. Open Questions\\n\\n1. Specific authentication mechanism for multiple repositories\\n2. Detailed conflict resolution strategy beyond current scope\\n3. Performance tuning for large repositories\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThis architecture provides a robust, performant solution for git repository synchronization, meeting all specified requirements while maintaining flexibility for future enhancements."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Wr8ZNGZqqERoP2aMFcxywm', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tdd_coordinator_model_validation_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Wr8ZNGZqqERoP2aMFcxywm', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# TDD Coordinator Model Validation Requirements\\n\\n## Objective\\nValidate performance improvements for TDD Coordinator by transitioning from claude-3-5-haiku-20241022 to claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\\n\\n## Performance Metrics\\n- Current Model: claude-3-5-haiku-20241022\\n- Target Model: claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\\n- Expected Improvement: 50% success rate\\n\\n## Validation Criteria\\n1. Benchmark current model performance\\n2. Migrate to new model\\n3. Compare performance metrics\\n4. Verify improvement meets or exceeds 50% success rate\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Full system redesign\\n- Changes to underlying test generation logic\\n\\n## Success Definition\\n- Performance improvement of 50% or more\\n- No regression in existing test coverage\\n- Minimal disruption to current workflow"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_015CPCnLr5Uyq737hWr1tQFp', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Backend Tasks - Performance Benchmarking\n\n## Milestone Overview\nEstablish baseline performance metrics for current haiku model (claude-3-5-haiku-20241022) in TDD Coordinator to prepare for model validation and comparison with claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929.\n\n## Backend Components Identified\n\n### 1. Performance Metrics Collection System\n- API endpoints for capturing TDD Coordinator execution metrics\n- Database schema for storing performance data\n- Background services for metric aggregation\n\n### 2. Model Performance Tracking Database\n- Schema for storing model execution results\n- Time-series data for trend analysis\n- Performance comparison capabilities\n\n### 3. Benchmarking API Layer\n- REST endpoints for triggering benchmark runs\n- Real-time performance monitoring\n- Historical data retrieval\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Priority 1: Foundation Tasks\n\n#### Task 1: Design Performance Metrics Database Schema\n**Description**: Create database models to capture comprehensive TDD Coordinator performance metrics including success rates, execution times, error types, and test generation quality.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Database tables for: benchmark_runs, model_executions, performance_metrics, error_logs\n- Schema supports both haiku and sonnet model data\n- Indexes on timestamp, model_name, success_rate for efficient querying\n- Migration scripts created and tested\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n#### Task 2: Implement Performance Metrics Collection API\n**Description**: Build REST API endpoints to receive and store performance data from TDD Coordinator executions.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- POST /api/v1/metrics/execution - Record single execution result\n- POST /api/v1/metrics/batch - Record multiple executions\n- GET /api/v1/metrics/summary - Retrieve aggregated performance data\n- Input validation using Pydantic models\n- Error handling and logging implemented\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n#### Task 3: Create Benchmark Execution Service\n**Description**: Implement background service to orchestrate benchmark runs against current haiku model using standardized test scenarios.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Service can execute predefined benchmark scenarios\n- Captures timing, success/failure, and quality metrics\n- Handles concurrent benchmark execution\n- Stores results via metrics collection API\n- Configurable benchmark parameters\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 2\n**Complexity**: Complex\n\n### Priority 2: Data Analysis and Reporting\n\n#### Task 4: Implement Performance Analytics API\n**Description**: Build API endpoints to retrieve and analyze performance metrics for baseline establishment and comparison.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- GET /api/v1/analytics/baseline - Current model baseline metrics\n- GET /api/v1/analytics/trends - Performance trends over time\n- GET /api/v1/analytics/comparison - Compare model performance\n- Statistical calculations (mean, median, percentiles)\n- Data aggregation by time periods\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 2\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n#### Task 5: Create Benchmark Configuration Management\n**Description**: Implement API for managing benchmark test scenarios and configuration parameters.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- CRUD operations for benchmark scenarios\n- Version control for test configurations\n- Import/export benchmark definitions\n- Validation of scenario parameters\n- Default benchmark suite for TDD Coordinator validation\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n### Priority 3: Integration and Monitoring\n\n#### Task 6: Implement Real-time Performance Monitoring\n**Description**: Create real-time monitoring capabilities for ongoing TDD Coordinator performance tracking.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- WebSocket endpoint for live performance updates\n- Performance alerts for degradation detection\n- Dashboard API endpoints for real-time metrics\n- Configurable thresholds for performance alerts\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 4\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n#### Task 7: Build Model Comparison Framework\n**Description**: Implement backend services to support A/B testing and performance comparison between haiku and sonnet models.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Side-by-side execution framework\n- Statistical significance testing\n- Performance delta calculations\n- Automated comparison reporting\n- Support for multiple model versions\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 4, Task 3\n**Complexity**: Complex\n\n### Priority 4: Data Export and Reporting\n\n#### Task 8: Create Performance Report Generation API\n**Description**: Build API endpoints for generating comprehensive performance reports and data exports.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Generate baseline performance reports\n- Export data in multiple formats (JSON, CSV)\n- Scheduled report generation\n- Custom date range filtering\n- Performance summary statistics\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 4\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n#### Task 9: Implement Data Retention and Archival\n**Description**: Create data lifecycle management for performance metrics with appropriate retention policies.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Automated data archival after configurable periods\n- Data compression for historical metrics\n- Purge policies for old benchmark data\n- Backup and restore capabilities\n- Performance optimization for large datasets\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n## Implementation Order\n\n### Phase 1: Core Infrastructure (Week 1)\n1. Task 1: Design Performance Metrics Database Schema\n2. Task 2: Implement Performance Metrics Collection API\n3. Task 5: Create Benchmark Configuration Management\n\n### Phase 2: Benchmarking Engine (Week 2)\n4. Task 3: Create Benchmark Execution Service\n5. Task 4: Implement Performance Analytics API\n\n### Phase 3: Advanced Features (Week 3)\n6. Task 8: Create Performance Report Generation API\n7. Task 6: Implement Real-time Performance Monitoring\n8. Task 7: Build Model Comparison Framework\n\n### Phase 4: Operations (Week 4)\n9. Task 9: Implement Data Retention and Archival\n\n## Technical Specifications\n\n### Database Models\n```python\nclass BenchmarkRun(BaseModel):\n    id: int\n    model_name: str\n    run_timestamp: datetime\n    scenario_id: int\n    success_count: int\n    failure_count: int\n    avg_execution_time: float\n    \nclass ModelExecution(BaseModel):\n    id: int\n    benchmark_run_id: int\n    execution_timestamp: datetime\n    success: bool\n    execution_time_ms: int\n    error_type: Optional[str]\n    test_quality_score: Optional[float]\n```\n\n### API Endpoints Summary\n- `/api/v1/metrics/*` - Performance data collection\n- `/api/v1/analytics/*` - Performance analysis and reporting\n- `/api/v1/benchmarks/*` - Benchmark configuration and execution\n- `/api/v1/reports/*` - Report generation and export\n\n## Dependencies Map\n```\nTask 1 → Task 2 → Task 3 → Task 7\nTask 1 → Task 9\nTask 2 → Task 4 → Task 6\nTask 2 → Task 4 → Task 7\nTask 4 → Task 8\nTask 5 (independent)\n```\n\n## Estimated Timeline\n- **Total Effort**: 4 weeks\n- **Critical Path**: Task 1 → Task 2 → Task 3 → Task 7 (2.5 weeks)\n- **Parallel Work**: Configuration management, reporting, monitoring can be developed in parallel\n\n## Success Metrics\n- All API endpoints tested with >95% code coverage\n- Baseline metrics collection operational for haiku model\n- Performance comparison framework ready for sonnet model integration\n- Database can handle 10,000+ benchmark executions efficiently'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_015CPCnLr5Uyq737hWr1tQFp', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1_20260116_224406.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1_20260116_224406.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Backend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks backend milestones into specific API, database, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify backend components, endpoints, data models, and business logic. Coordinates backend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break backend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Backend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**API Style**: REST with JSON, OpenAPI docs\n**Framework**: FastAPI (Python) or Express (Node.js)\n**Database**: PostgreSQL with SQLAlchemy/Prisma ORM\n**Auth**: JWT tokens, bcrypt password hashing\n**Validation**: Pydantic (Python) or Joi (Node.js)\n**Testing**: pytest or Jest with coverage\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all backend components:\n  * API endpoints (REST, GraphQL)\n  * Database models/schemas\n  * Business logic services\n  * Authentication/authorization\n  * Background jobs/workers\n  * External API integrations\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (how to know it\'s done)\nDependencies (what must be done first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by Priority**\nGroup related tasks together\nOrder by dependencies (foundational → features)\nIdentify critical path tasks\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Backend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Business logic is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "calculate shipping" without formula)\n- **Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., sync vs async processing)\n- **Data relationships are contradictory** (e.g., conflicting schema requirements)\n- **Security/compliance requirements are ambiguous** (e.g., PII handling rules)\n- **NOT for**: standard tech choices, common patterns, typical implementations\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All backend tasks identified and documented\n- Task dependencies mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 94.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.8\n- Common errors to avoid: RateLimitError, CircuitBreakerOpenError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: RateLimitError, CircuitBreakerOpenError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
