{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 22:44:12", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-a7c9b551-56a5-43de-9ba6-ea7bf396b064', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Logs Agents Tab Implementation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01UdLTe1wQho5z7at4SoFXsw', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01UdLTe1wQho5z7at4SoFXsw', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Requirements Document: Logs & Agents Tab Implementation\\n\\n## Project Vision\\nImplement a comprehensive \\"Logs & Agents\\" tab for the Ensemble UI that provides real-time backend log monitoring and agent definition file management capabilities. This will enable users to monitor system behavior in real-time and manage agent configurations through a user-friendly interface.\\n\\n## Core Objectives\\n1. **Real-time Log Streaming**: Enable users to view backend logs as they happen\\n2. **Agent File Management**: Provide a file explorer for viewing and editing agent definitions\\n3. **Seamless Integration**: Add new functionality without disrupting existing UI\\n4. **Performance Safety**: Ensure log streaming doesn\'t degrade system performance\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### F1: Backend Log Streaming\\n- **F1.1**: Create WebSocket endpoint `/ws/logs` for real-time log streaming\\n- **F1.2**: Implement log buffer with 1000-entry limit for memory safety\\n- **F1.3**: Structure log entries with timestamp, level, agent_id, request_id, message\\n- **F1.4**: Support server-side filtering by log level (INFO, WARNING, ERROR, DEBUG)\\n- **F1.5**: Support server-side filtering by agent_id and request_id\\n- **F1.6**: Maintain existing logging functionality without performance degradation\\n\\n### F2: Frontend Log Viewer\\n- **F2.1**: Create LogStreamPanel component with WebSocket connection\\n- **F2.2**: Implement auto-scroll with toggle functionality\\n- **F2.3**: Provide log level filter buttons (INFO, WARNING, ERROR, DEBUG)\\n- **F2.4**: Include search filter for agent_id/request_id\\n- **F2.5**: Support pause/resume streaming controls\\n- **F2.6**: Provide clear logs functionality\\n- **F2.7**: Implement color coding by log level\\n- **F2.8**: Display timestamps with relative/absolute toggle\\n\\n### F3: Agent Definition Explorer\\n- **F3.1**: Create AgentExplorer component with tree-view structure\\n- **F3.2**: Display directories: leadership/, coordinators/, developers/, testers/, designers/\\n- **F3.3**: Support collapsible/expandable directories\\n- **F3.4**: Enable file selection with visual feedback\\n- **F3.5**: Use existing `/api/agents` endpoint for data\\n- **F3.6**: Differentiate files and folders with appropriate icons\\n\\n### F4: Agent Definition Editor\\n- **F4.1**: Create AgentDefinitionViewer component with read-only default view\\n- **F4.2**: Implement edit mode toggle with textarea editing\\n- **F4.3**: Provide markdown preview panel\\n- **F4.4**: Integrate with existing `/api/agents/update` endpoint for saving\\n- **F4.5**: Implement automatic backup functionality\\n- **F4.6**: Provide revert functionality using backups\\n- **F4.7**: Display success/error feedback for save operations\\n\\n### F5: Tab Integration\\n- **F5.1**: Add tab navigation to App.jsx with \\"Main View\\" and \\"Logs & Agents\\" tabs\\n- **F5.2**: Preserve all existing functionality in \\"Main View\\" tab\\n- **F5.3**: Implement split-pane layout in \\"Logs & Agents\\" tab\\n- **F5.4**: Ensure responsive design across screen sizes\\n- **F5.5**: Maintain consistent dark theme styling\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### NF1: Performance\\n- Log streaming must not degrade backend performance\\n- WebSocket connections should be efficiently managed\\n- Log buffer must not exceed memory constraints (1000 entries)\\n\\n### NF2: Usability\\n- UI must follow existing design patterns and dark theme\\n- Components must be responsive across different screen sizes\\n- Interface should be intuitive for developers and administrators\\n\\n### NF3: Reliability\\n- WebSocket connections should handle disconnections gracefully\\n- File editing should include backup/recovery mechanisms\\n- Error states should be clearly communicated to users\\n\\n### NF4: Maintainability\\n- Code should follow existing project conventions\\n- Components should be modular and reusable\\n- TDD methodology must be followed (tests before implementation)\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Must use existing WebSocket infrastructure (building on `/ws/agent-status`)\\n- Must use React Bootstrap for UI consistency\\n- Must integrate with existing API endpoints (`/api/agents`, `/api/agents/{tier}/{name}`, `/api/agents/update`)\\n- Must use simple textarea for editing (no Monaco editor requirement)\\n- Must use CSS flexbox for split-pane layout\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. Users can view real-time backend logs without page refresh\\n2. Log streaming includes filtering by level and search terms\\n3. Users can browse agent definition files in intuitive tree structure\\n4. Users can view and edit agent definitions with automatic backup\\n5. Tab integration preserves existing functionality\\n6. System performance remains stable under normal log volume\\n7. All tests pass (following TDD methodology)\\n8. UI maintains consistency with existing design\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Advanced log analysis or aggregation features\\n- Complex code editing features (syntax highlighting, IntelliSense)\\n- User authentication/authorization for file editing\\n- Log persistence to database\\n- Advanced layout customization options\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- Existing WebSocket infrastructure (`/ws/agent-status`)\\n- Existing agent API endpoints\\n- React Bootstrap framework\\n- Current dark theme CSS\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n- Standard log volumes won\'t exceed buffer capacity under normal operation\\n- Users have appropriate permissions for file system access\\n- Existing API endpoints provide sufficient data for agent management\\n- WebSocket infrastructure can handle additional concurrent connections\\n- Current UI framework (React Bootstrap) is sufficient for new components\\n\\n## Testing Requirements\\nFollowing TDD methodology:\\n1. Unit tests for all React components\\n2. Integration tests for WebSocket connections\\n3. API integration tests for agent management\\n4. End-to-end tests for complete user workflows\\n5. Performance tests for log streaming under load"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01LJsQXBLduVYqPimeDBvVEk', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Logs Agents Tab Implementation', 'description': 'Implement Logs & Agents Tab with real-time log streaming and agent file management'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01LJsQXBLduVYqPimeDBvVEk', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "23ed529f", "message": "Created project: Logs Agents Tab Implementation", "summary": {"project_id": "23ed529f", "project_name": "Logs Agents Tab Implementation", "description": "Implement Logs & Agents Tab with real-time log streaming and agent file management", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T22:42:47.743212", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T22:42:47.743212", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T22:42:47.743212", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Logs Agents Tab Implementation\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01VRtiX2VfeCKkcMwC8QnX7T', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01VRtiX2VfeCKkcMwC8QnX7T', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "completed", "response_type": "conversational", "message": "Now I\'ll analyze these requirements and design a comprehensive architecture. The project needs to implement a family-based naming and achievement system for agent groups. Let me create a detailed architecture proposal:", "agent": "System Architect"}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01RMaaztMMSByUGpa8TycxeE', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Milestone Plan: Logs & Agents Tab Implementation\n\n## Milestone 1: Backend WebSocket Log Streaming (2-3 days)\n### Objectives\n- Implement `/ws/logs` WebSocket endpoint\n- Create log buffering mechanism\n- Develop server-side filtering capabilities\n\n### Deliverables\n- WebSocket log streaming implementation\n- Log entry data structure\n- Server-side filtering logic\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Log entries have correct timestamp, level, agent_id, request_id\n- 1000-entry log buffer\n- Filtering by log level and agent_id works\n\n## Milestone 2: Frontend Log Viewer (3-4 days)\n### Objectives\n- Create LogStreamPanel React component\n- Implement WebSocket connection\n- Develop log viewing controls\n\n### Deliverables\n- LogStreamPanel component\n- Log level and search filtering\n- Auto-scroll and streaming controls\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Real-time log display\n- Pause/resume functionality\n- Color-coded log levels\n- Responsive design\n\n## Milestone 3: Agent Definition Explorer & Editor (3-4 days)\n### Objectives\n- Implement AgentExplorer with tree-view\n- Create AgentDefinitionViewer\n- Enable file selection and editing\n\n### Deliverables\n- AgentExplorer component\n- Agent file selection mechanism\n- Read/edit functionality with backups\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Tree-view of agent directories\n- File selection with visual feedback\n- Edit mode with markdown preview\n- Backup and revert functionality\n\n## Milestone 4: Tab Integration & Final Testing (2-3 days)\n### Objectives\n- Add new tab to main application\n- Integrate all components\n- Comprehensive testing\n\n### Deliverables\n- Updated App.jsx with new tab\n- Complete system integration\n- Full test coverage\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- New tab works without breaking existing functionality\n- All components integrated\n- All tests pass\n- Performance maintained\n\n## Dependencies\n1. Milestone 1 must complete before Milestone 2\n2. Milestone 2 must complete before Milestone 3\n3. All previous milestones must complete before Milestone 4\n\n## Total Estimated Timeline: 10-14 days'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01RMaaztMMSByUGpa8TycxeE', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_224412.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_224412.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour