{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 22:44:16", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-d1ceeeec-afa2-405f-954f-7c0cea8bad82', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Core Infrastructure & Remote Operations - Establish foundational sync capabilities with remote repository connection management, basic fetch/pull operations, configuration system integration, and core error handling framework",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/github-bots/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Wj1xnY8G4f9SkKxYMZiGGe', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Wj1xnY8G4f9SkKxYMZiGGe', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture Proposal: Design Phase Pause Fix Implementation\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Problem Being Solved\\nA critical bug in the agent pipeline that incorrectly terminates execution when an agent returns a `needs_user_input` status. The new architecture will enable graceful pausing, user interaction, and continuation of agent workflows.\\n\\n### Architectural Pattern\\n- **Style**: Event-Driven Async Microservice Architecture\\n- **Core Pattern**: State Machine with Continuation Context\\n\\n## 2. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Backend\\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\\n- **Web Framework**: FastAPI\\n- **Async Processing**: `asyncio`, FastAPI BackgroundTasks\\n- **Testing**: pytest, pytest-asyncio\\n\\n### State Management\\n- **In-Memory State**: Enhanced dictionary with thread-safe state tracking\\n- **Continuation Context**: Dataclass-based context storage\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### 3.1 Agent Execution Engine\\n```\\n[Agent Orchestrator]\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 _execute_agent_background (MODIFIED)\\n    \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Detect needs_user_input status\\n    \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Store continuation context\\n    \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Update agent state\\n    \\u2502\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 continue_agent_with_answer (NEW)\\n    \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Retrieve stored context\\n    \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Spawn new agent\\n    \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Inject previous context\\n    \\u2502\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 State Tracking\\n        \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 active_agents dictionary\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Async state transitions\\n```\\n\\n### 3.2 Question Handling Flow\\n```\\n[User Interaction]\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Agent returns needs_user_input\\n    \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Store question_id\\n    \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Pause agent execution\\n    \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Mark as awaiting_user_input\\n    \\u2502\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 User provides answer\\n    \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Match to question_id\\n    \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Retrieve continuation context\\n    \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Trigger agent continuation\\n```\\n\\n## 4. Data Structures\\n\\n### Agent State Model\\n```python\\nclass AgentState:\\n    status: Literal[\'running\', \'awaiting_user_input\', \'completed\']\\n    awaiting_question_id: Optional[str]\\n    continuation_context: Dict[str, Any]\\n```\\n\\n## 5. API Design\\n\\n### Key Endpoints\\n- `POST /answer_question`\\n  - Input: `{question_id: str, answer: Any}`\\n  - Process: Async agent continuation\\n  - Returns: Continuation status\\n\\n## 6. Error Handling Strategy\\n- Graceful handling of:\\n  - Missing agents\\n  - Invalid question_ids\\n  - Continuation context retrieval failures\\n\\n## 7. Testing Approach\\n\\n### Test Pyramid\\n- Unit Tests (70%): Individual method behaviors\\n- Integration Tests (20%): Full workflow scenarios\\n- End-to-End Tests (10%): Complete agent pipeline\\n\\n## 8. Deployment Considerations\\n- Stateless design\\n- No persistent storage for paused agents\\n- Can be deployed in containerized environments\\n\\n## 9. Risks & Mitigations\\n\\n### Potential Risks\\n1. **Context Loss on Restart**\\n   - Mitigation: Clear documentation of stateless nature\\n2. **Race Conditions**\\n   - Mitigation: Strict question_id matching, async processing\\n\\n## 10. Open Questions\\n- Future support for persistent agent pausing?\\n- Multiple concurrent question handling?\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n1. Full state machine framework\\n2. Redis-backed continuation storage\\n3. Callback-based approach\\n\\n**Chosen Approach**: Lightweight, async-native solution maximizing simplicity and performance"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01FkAEgw6Doj8j22wwbu3WGs', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/github-bots/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01FkAEgw6Doj8j22wwbu3WGs', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# GitHub Sync Bot Requirements\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n- **Milestone**: 2 of 6 in GitHub Bots Suite\\n- **Purpose**: Implement advanced git synchronization capabilities\\n\\n## Core Capabilities\\n1. Remote Synchronization\\n   - Fetch and pull operations from remote repositories\\n   - Support for multiple remote repositories\\n   \\n2. Branch Management\\n   - Rebase operations with robust conflict handling\\n   - Safe stash management (save, restore, list)\\n   \\n3. Error Handling\\n   - Detailed conflict detection\\n   - Clear error reporting\\n   - Preservation of uncommitted changes\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- \\u2713 Successfully rebase branch with upstream changes\\n- \\u2713 Safely stash uncommitted changes before sync\\n- \\u2713 Detect and report conflicts clearly\\n- \\u2713 Restore stashed changes after successful sync\\n- \\u2713 Complete operations within 30 seconds for typical repositories\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Use existing base classes and configuration system\\n- Implement using Test-Driven Development (TDD)\\n- Comprehensive error handling\\n- Logging of all synchronization events\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Full repository migration\\n- Complex merge conflict resolution\\n- Support for non-git version control systems\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Base git configuration and authentication are already set up\\n- Typical repository size is under 1GB\\n- Standard git workflow (single branch, linear history)"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01VSHrqq2v533cMgzoFj4Q39', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Backend Tasks - Core Infrastructure & Remote Operations\n\n## Milestone Overview\nEstablish foundational sync capabilities with remote repository connection management, basic fetch/pull operations, configuration system integration, and core error handling framework.\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Phase 1: Core Infrastructure (Foundation)\n\n#### Task 1.1: Remote Repository Connection Management\n**Description**: Create service for managing multiple remote repository connections with authentication handling\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Support for multiple remote URLs (origin, upstream, etc.)\n- Secure credential storage/retrieval\n- Connection validation and health checks\n- Support for HTTPS and SSH authentication\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n#### Task 1.2: Git Configuration System Integration\n**Description**: Integrate with existing configuration system for git settings and repository preferences\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Read/write git configuration (user.name, user.email)\n- Repository-specific settings management\n- Default remote configuration\n- Configuration validation\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n#### Task 1.3: Core Error Handling Framework\n**Description**: Establish comprehensive error handling for git operations with detailed error classification\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Custom exception classes for git errors\n- Error categorization (network, auth, conflict, etc.)\n- Structured error responses with actionable messages\n- Error logging and monitoring integration\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n### Phase 2: Basic Git Operations\n\n#### Task 2.1: Git Repository Service\n**Description**: Core service for basic git repository operations and state management\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Repository initialization and validation\n- Working directory state checking\n- Branch status information\n- Repository metadata retrieval\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1, Task 1.3\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n#### Task 2.2: Fetch Operations API\n**Description**: Implement fetch operations for retrieving updates from remote repositories\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Fetch from specific remotes\n- Fetch all remotes\n- Progress tracking for large fetches\n- Bandwidth optimization (shallow fetch when appropriate)\n**Dependencies**: Task 2.1\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n#### Task 2.3: Pull Operations with Conflict Detection\n**Description**: Implement pull operations with robust conflict detection and reporting\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Fast-forward pulls when possible\n- Merge conflict detection and detailed reporting\n- Preserve local changes during conflicts\n- Rollback capability for failed pulls\n**Dependencies**: Task 2.2\n**Complexity**: Complex\n\n### Phase 3: Synchronization Foundation\n\n#### Task 3.1: Repository State Management\n**Description**: Service to track and manage repository state during sync operations\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Track working directory changes\n- Monitor staged/unstaged files\n- Detect uncommitted changes\n- State persistence during operations\n**Dependencies**: Task 2.1\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n#### Task 3.2: Stash Management System\n**Description**: Safe stash management for preserving uncommitted changes during sync operations\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Create stashes with descriptive names\n- List and manage multiple stashes\n- Apply stashes with conflict detection\n- Clean up temporary stashes\n**Dependencies**: Task 3.1\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n#### Task 3.3: Basic Rebase Foundation\n**Description**: Foundation for rebase operations (preparation for full rebase in future milestones)\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Validate rebase prerequisites\n- Detect rebase conflicts early\n- Safe rebase initiation\n- Rebase status monitoring\n**Dependencies**: Task 3.2, Task 2.3\n**Complexity**: Complex\n\n### Phase 4: API Layer\n\n#### Task 4.1: Remote Operations REST API\n**Description**: FastAPI endpoints for remote repository operations\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- GET /remotes - list configured remotes\n- POST /remotes - add/update remote configurations\n- DELETE /remotes/{name} - remove remote\n- GET /remotes/{name}/status - check remote connectivity\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1, Task 1.2\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n#### Task 4.2: Sync Operations REST API\n**Description**: FastAPI endpoints for synchronization operations\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- POST /sync/fetch - fetch from remotes\n- POST /sync/pull - pull with merge/rebase options\n- GET /sync/status - current sync operation status\n- POST /sync/cancel - cancel ongoing operation\n**Dependencies**: Task 2.2, Task 2.3\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n#### Task 4.3: Repository State REST API\n**Description**: FastAPI endpoints for repository state queries and management\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- GET /repo/status - comprehensive repository status\n- GET /repo/changes - list uncommitted changes\n- POST /repo/stash - create stash\n- GET /repo/stashes - list stashes\n**Dependencies**: Task 3.1, Task 3.2\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n### Phase 5: Integration & Testing Infrastructure\n\n#### Task 5.1: Async Background Task Management\n**Description**: Background task system for long-running git operations\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- FastAPI BackgroundTasks integration\n- Operation progress tracking\n- Task cancellation support\n- Resource cleanup on completion/failure\n**Dependencies**: Task 4.2\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n#### Task 5.2: Operation Logging and Monitoring\n**Description**: Comprehensive logging system for all git operations\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Structured logging with operation context\n- Performance metrics collection\n- Error tracking and aggregation\n- Debug mode with detailed git command logging\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.3\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n#### Task 5.3: Test Infrastructure Setup\n**Description**: Testing framework setup for git operations with mock repositories\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Mock git repository fixtures\n- Integration test helpers\n- Async test support\n- Git operation mocking utilities\n**Dependencies**: All previous tasks\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n## Task Dependencies Map\n\n```\nPhase 1 Foundation:\n├── Task 1.1 (Remote Connection) → Task 1.2 (Config Integration)\n├── Task 1.3 (Error Handling) → Independent\n└── Phase 1 → Phase 2\n\nPhase 2 Git Operations:\n├── Task 2.1 (Git Service) → Depends on 1.1, 1.3\n├── Task 2.2 (Fetch) → Depends on 2.1\n└── Task 2.3 (Pull) → Depends on 2.2\n\nPhase 3 Sync Foundation:\n├── Task 3.1 (State Management) → Depends on 2.1\n├── Task 3.2 (Stash) → Depends on 3.1\n└── Task 3.3 (Rebase Foundation) → Depends on 3.2, 2.3\n\nPhase 4 API Layer:\n├── Task 4.1 (Remote API) → Depends on 1.1, 1.2\n├── Task 4.2 (Sync API) → Depends on 2.2, 2.3\n└── Task 4.3 (State API) → Depends on 3.1, 3.2\n\nPhase 5 Integration:\n├── Task 5.1 (Background Tasks) → Depends on 4.2\n├── Task 5.2 (Logging) → Depends on 1.3\n└── Task 5.3 (Test Infrastructure) → Depends on all previous\n```\n\n## Critical Path\n1. Task 1.1 (Remote Connection) → 1.3 (Error Handling) → 2.1 (Git Service) → 2.2 (Fetch) → 2.3 (Pull) → 3.1 (State Management) → 3.2 (Stash) → 4.2 (Sync API) → 5.1 (Background Tasks)\n\n## Estimated Timeline\n- **Total Tasks**: 15\n- **Simple Tasks**: 5 (1-2 days each)\n- **Medium Tasks**: 7 (2-4 days each)\n- **Complex Tasks**: 3 (4-6 days each)\n- **Estimated Total**: 35-50 development days\n\n## Next Steps\nReady for handoff to TDD Coordinator for implementation. Tasks are ordered by dependency and complexity, with clear acceptance criteria for each component.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01VSHrqq2v533cMgzoFj4Q39', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1_20260116_224416.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1_20260116_224416.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Backend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks backend milestones into specific API, database, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify backend components, endpoints, data models, and business logic. Coordinates backend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break backend work into actionable