ss": true, "content": "# Tmux Monitoring Dashboard - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Architectural Pattern\\n**Monitoring Dashboard with Modular Components**\\n- **Type**: Terminal-based Monitoring System\\n- **Pattern**: Microservice-inspired modular design\\n- **Core Philosophy**: Separation of Concerns with Lightweight Integration\\n\\n### High-Level Architecture\\n1. **Session Management Layer**: Tmux Session Creation/Control\\n2. **Monitoring Components**:\\n   - CLI Interface Pane\\n   - Logging Pane\\n   - File Browser Pane\\n   - Task Tracking Pane\\n3. **Background Services**:\\n   - Task Watcher\\n   - Log Streamer\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n### Core Technologies\\n- **Terminal Multiplexer**: Tmux (v3.0+)\\n- **Scripting Languages**: \\n  - Bash (Session Management)\\n  - Python 3.8+ (Task Watching, Advanced Processing)\\n- **Text Editor**: Vim (with netrw/NERDTree)\\n\\n### Supporting Tools\\n- **File Watching**: \\n  - `inotifywait` (Linux)\\n  - `fswatch` (macOS)\\n- **Log Processing**: \\n  - `tail`\\n  - Python\'s `watchdog` library (optional)\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### 1. start_monitor.sh\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Create tmux session\\n- Configure 2x2 layout\\n- Launch individual panes\\n- Handle session persistence\\n\\n**Key Functions**:\\n```bash\\ncreate_tmux_session() {\\n  tmux new-session -d -s ensemble-monitor\\n  setup_panes\\n  configure_pane_contents\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### 2. task_watcher.py\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Monitor project state file\\n- Parse task statuses\\n- Generate formatted task list\\n- Refresh on interval\\n\\n**Key Methods**:\\n```python\\ndef watch_project_state():\\n    # Watch ~/.ensemble/projects/{project_id}/project.json\\n    while True:\\n        update_task_list()\\n        time.sleep(REFRESH_INTERVAL)\\n\\ndef update_task_list():\\n    # Read JSON, categorize tasks\\n    # Render to tmux pane\\n```\\n\\n### 3. log_streamer.sh\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Stream backend logs\\n- Handle log rotation\\n- Provide real-time view\\n\\n**Key Functions**:\\n```bash\\nstream_logs() {\\n  tail -f logs/backend.log | \\\\\\n    colorize_output | \\\\\\n    tmux load-buffer -\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Data Flow\\n\\n```\\n[Project State] \\n    \\u2193\\ntask_watcher.py \\n    \\u2193\\n[Formatted Task List]\\n    \\u2193\\nTmux Pane 4\\n```\\n\\n```\\n[Backend Logs] \\n    \\u2193\\nlog_streamer.sh \\n    \\u2193\\n[Colorized/Formatted Logs]\\n    \\u2193\\nTmux Pane 2\\n```\\n\\n## Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Installation\\n1. Copy scripts to `scripts/deployment/`\\n2. Ensure executable permissions\\n3. Add to PATH or use full path\\n\\n### Execution\\n```bash\\n# Launch dashboard\\n./start_monitor.sh\\n\\n# Stop dashboard\\n./stop_monitor.sh\\n```\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Component Testing\\n- Unit test each script independently\\n- Mock tmux interactions\\n- Validate output formatting\\n\\n### Integration Testing\\n- Test full dashboard launch\\n- Verify pane interactions\\n- Check log streaming\\n- Validate task list updates\\n\\n## Configuration\\n\\n### Environment Variables\\n- `ENSEMBLE_PROJECT_ID`: Select project to monitor\\n- `TMUX_LOG_PATH`: Custom log file location\\n- `TASK_REFRESH_INTERVAL`: Update frequency\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk: Performance Overhead\\n**Mitigation**: \\n- Use efficient polling intervals\\n- Implement lightweight parsing\\n- Consider compiled Python or Go for task watching\\n\\n### Risk: tmux Version Compatibility\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Detect tmux version\\n- Provide fallback configurations\\n- Clear version requirements in documentation\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Alternative 1: Web-based Dashboard\\n**Pros**: \\n- Rich visualizations\\n- Remote access\\n\\n**Cons**:\\n- Increased complexity\\n- Requires web server\\n- Less terminal-native\\n\\n### Alternative 2: Separate Terminal Windows\\n**Pros**: \\n- Simple to implement\\n- No tmux dependency\\n\\n**Cons**:\\n- Context switching\\n- Manual window management\\n- Less integrated\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\n1. Log parsing strategy (raw vs. structured)\\n2. Error handling for missing project files\\n3. Customization options for different workflows\\n\\n## Roadmap\\n\\n### MVP (Milestone 1)\\n- Basic tmux layout\\n- Simple log streaming\\n- Static task list\\n\\n### V2 \\n- Dynamic task updates\\n- Enhanced log parsing\\n- Configurable views\\n\\n## Compliance Checklist\\n\\u2705 Single-command launch\\n\\u2705 Real-time task tracking\\n\\u2705 Log streaming\\n\\u2705 File browser integration\\n\\u2705 Supports macOS/Linux\\n\\u2705 Minimal external dependencies\\n\\n## Recommended Next Steps\\n1. Implement start_monitor.sh\\n2. Develop task_watcher.py\\n3. Create comprehensive test suite\\n4. Document usage and configuration"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01RtEHTRrVY981C5PdnM1d8C', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Backend Tasks - Develop core monitoring scripts and task watcher prototype\n\n## Overview\nBreaking down Milestone 1 for the tmux monitoring dashboard backend components. This milestone focuses on core monitoring scripts and task watcher prototype implementation.\n\n## Backend Components Identified\n\n### Core Scripts and Services\n1. **Session Management**: Bash scripts for tmux session control\n2. **Task Watcher Service**: Python service for monitoring project state\n3. **Log Streaming Service**: Bash service for real-time log streaming\n4. **Configuration Management**: Environment-based configuration system\n\n---\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Foundation Tasks (Priority 1)\n\n#### Task 1: Project State Data Model\n- **Description**: Define the project state JSON schema and file structure that will be monitored by the task watcher\n- **Acceptance Criteria**: \n  - JSON schema defined for project.json structure\n  - Sample project state file created for testing\n  - Schema includes tasks with id, name, status, assigned_to, dependencies\n  - File location standardized at `~/.ensemble/projects/{project_id}/project.json`\n- **Dependencies**: None\n- **Complexity**: Simple\n\n#### Task 2: Environment Configuration System\n- **Description**: Create configuration management for environment variables and default settings\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  - Support for ENSEMBLE_PROJECT_ID, TMUX_LOG_PATH, TASK_REFRESH_INTERVAL\n  - Default value handling for missing environment variables\n  - Configuration validation and error handling\n  - Cross-platform compatibility (macOS/Linux)\n- **Dependencies**: None\n- **Complexity**: Simple\n\n### Core Monitoring Services (Priority 2)\n\n#### Task 3: Task Watcher Python Service\n- **Description**: Build the core task monitoring service that watches project state files and formats task output\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  - Python service that monitors project.json file changes\n  - Real-time file watching using appropriate library (watchdog or inotify)\n  - Parse JSON and categorize tasks by status (todo, in_progress, completed, blocked)\n  - Format task list for tmux pane display\n  - Configurable refresh intervals\n  - Error handling for malformed JSON or missing files\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1, Task 2\n- **Complexity**: Medium\n\n#### Task 4: Log Streaming Service\n- **Description**: Create bash service for streaming and formatting backend logs\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  - Bash script that uses `tail -f` for log streaming\n  - Log colorization for different log levels (INFO, WARN, ERROR)\n  - Handle log rotation gracefully\n  - Buffer output for tmux pane integration\n  - Support for custom log file paths via environment variables\n- **Dependencies**: Task 2\n- **Complexity**: Simple\n\n### Tmux Integration Layer (Priority 3)\n\n#### Task 5: Tmux Session Manager Script\n- **Description**: Build the main session management script that creates and configures the monitoring dashboard\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  - Bash script `start_monitor.sh` that creates tmux session\n  - Configure 2x2 pane layout as specified in architecture\n  - Launch task watcher in designated pane\n  - Launch log streamer in designated pane\n  - Setup CLI interface and file browser panes\n  - Session naming and conflict handling\n  - Cross-platform tmux command compatibility\n- **Dependencies**: Task 3, Task 4\n- **Complexity**: Medium\n\n#### Task 6: Pane Content Management\n- **Description**: Implement the logic for managing content in each tmux pane\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  - Pane 1: CLI interface with vim/editor setup\n  - Pane 2: Log streaming display\n  - Pane 3: File browser (vim netrw or equivalent)\n  - Pane 4: Task list display\n  - Proper content routing to correct panes\n  - Pane refresh and update mechanisms\n- **Dependencies**: Task 5\n- **Complexity**: Medium\n\n### Testing and Utilities (Priority 4)\n\n#### Task 7: Session Cleanup Script\n- **Description**: Create script for properly stopping and cleaning up the monitoring dashboard\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  - `stop_monitor.sh` script that kills tmux session\n  - Graceful shutdown of background processes\n  - Cleanup of temporary files\n  - Session detection and validation\n- **Dependencies**: Task 5\n- **Complexity**: Simple\n\n#### Task 8: Mock Data Generator\n- **Description**: Create utility for generating test project state data for development and testing\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  - Script to generate sample project.json files\n  - Various task states and scenarios for testing\n  - Configurable number of tasks and complexity\n  - Support for testing edge cases (missing files, malformed JSON)\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1\n- **Complexity**: Simple\n\n#### Task 9: Integration Test Suite\n- **Description**: Build test suite for validating the complete monitoring dashboard functionality\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  - Test tmux session creation and teardown\n  - Validate pane content routing\n  - Test task watcher responsiveness to file changes\n  - Test log streaming functionality\n  - Cross-platform compatibility testing\n  - Error scenario testing (missing files, permissions, etc.)\n- **Dependencies**: Task 5, Task 6, Task 8\n- **Complexity**: Complex\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Order\n\n1. **Foundation**: Tasks 1, 2 (Environment and data models)\n2. **Core Services**: Tasks 3, 4 (Task watcher and log streamer)\n3. **Integration**: Tasks 5, 6 (Tmux session management)\n4. **Quality**: Tasks 7, 8, 9 (Cleanup, testing, validation)\n\n## Technical Notes\n\n### File Watching Strategy\n- Linux: Use `inotifywait` for efficient file monitoring\n- macOS: Use `fswatch` as alternative\n- Python fallback: `watchdog` library for cross-platform compatibility\n\n### Performance Considerations\n- Default task refresh interval: 2 seconds\n- Efficient JSON parsing with error handling\n- Minimal memory footprint for continuous monitoring\n\n### Error Handling Strategy\n- Graceful degradation when project files are missing\n- Clear error messages in tmux panes\n- Automatic recovery when files become available\n\n## Dependencies Map\n```\nTask 1 (Project State) → Task 3 (Task Watcher) → Task 5 (Session Manager) → Task 6 (Pane Management) → Task 9 (Integration Tests)\nTask 2 (Configuration) → Task 4 (Log Streamer) ↗\nTask 1 → Task 8 (Mock Data) → Task 9\nTask 5 → Task 7 (Cleanup)\n```\n\n## Ready for TDD Implementation\nAll tasks are defined with clear acceptance criteria and can be implemented using Test-Driven Development approach by the TDD Coordinator.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01RtEHTRrVY981C5PdnM1d8C', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1_20260116_224452.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1_20260116_224452.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Backend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks backend milestones into specific API, database, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify backend components, endpoints, data models, and business logic. Coordinates backend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break backend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Backend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**API Style**: REST with JSON, OpenAPI docs\n**Framework**: FastAPI (Python) or Express (Node.js)\n**Database**: PostgreSQL with SQLAlchemy/Prisma ORM\n**Auth**: JWT tokens, bcrypt password hashing\n**Validation**: Pydantic (Python) or Joi (Node.js)\n**Testing**: pytest or Jest with coverage\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all backend components:\n  * API endpoints (REST, GraphQL)\n  * Database models/schemas\n  * Business logic services\n  * Authentication/authorization\n  * Background jobs/workers\n  * External API integrations\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (how to know it\'s done)\nDependencies (what must be done first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by Priority**\nGroup related tasks together\nOrder by dependencies (foundational → features)\nIdentify critical path tasks\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Backend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Business logic is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "calculate shipping" without formula)\n- **Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., sync vs async processing)\n- **Data relationships are contradictory** (e.g., conflicting schema requirements)\n- **Security/compliance requirements are ambiguous** (e.g., PII handling rules)\n- **NOT for**: standard tech choices, common patterns, typical implementations\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All backend tasks identified and documented\n- Task dependencies mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 94.3%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.9\n- Common errors to avoid: RateLimitError, CircuitBreakerOpenError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: RateLimitError, CircuitBreakerOpenError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
