{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 22:45:12", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-3454b5ba-2f9b-485c-b834-96632d6e1c14', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Core Infrastructure & Remote Operations - Establish foundational sync capabilities with remote repository connection management, basic fetch/pull operations, configuration system integration, and core error handling framework",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/github-bots/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01LwUxngHrUNQSmsVPiPbLfy', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01LwUxngHrUNQSmsVPiPbLfy', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Activity Tracking Fixes - System Architecture\\n\\n## A) Architecture Overview\\nA focused, surgical fix to the Ensemble UI activity tracking system. The architecture addresses three specific bugs preventing file generation tracking and request count updates with minimal system disruption and maximum backward compatibility.\\n\\n## B) Current System Analysis\\n\\n### Existing Components (Working Correctly)\\n- **ActivityTracker** (`src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`) - Core tracking logic works\\n- **Activity APIs** (`src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py`) - Endpoints correctly query tracker\\n- **Frontend Display** - UI correctly consumes API data\\n- **Agent Execution** - Agents successfully create files and complete tasks\\n\\n### Problem Areas (Requiring Fixes)\\n1. **WriteFileTool** - Doesn\'t record file generation to ActivityTracker\\n2. **Request Counting** - `increment_request_counts()` method never called\\n3. **File Discovery** - Limited to output directory only\\n\\n## C) Proposed Architecture Changes\\n\\n### 1. Enhanced WriteFileTool with Context Propagation\\n\\n**Current Architecture:**\\n```\\nAgentRuntime \\u2192 ToolRegistry \\u2192 WriteFileTool \\u2192 File System\\n                                    \\u2193\\n                              (No tracking)\\n```\\n\\n**Fixed Architecture:**\\n```\\nAgentRuntime \\u2192 ToolRegistry \\u2192 WriteFileTool \\u2192 File System\\n     \\u2193              \\u2193              \\u2193\\n Context Info \\u2192 Tracking Params \\u2192 ActivityTracker.record_file_generated()\\n```\\n\\n**Implementation Pattern:**\\n- **Context Injection**: Pass agent_id, request_id, agent_name through tool construction\\n- **Optional Parameters**: Maintain backward compatibility with optional tracking parameters\\n- **Error Isolation**: Wrap tracking calls in try-catch to prevent tool failures\\n\\n### 2. Auto-Increment Request Counters\\n\\n**Pattern:** Hook into existing activity recording methods\\n\\n```\\nrecord_agent_started() \\u2192 increment_request_counts(agents=+1)\\nrecord_file_generated() \\u2192 increment_request_counts(files=+1) \\nrecord_git_commit() \\u2192 increment_request_counts(commits=+1)\\n```\\n\\n**Thread Safety:** Leverage existing ActivityTracker synchronization mechanisms\\n\\n### 3. Enhanced File Discovery (Optional Enhancement)\\n\\n**Current:** Scan output directory only\\n**Enhanced:** Scan multiple directories with intelligent filtering\\n\\n```\\nFile Discovery Strategy:\\n- Output directory (priority 1)\\n- Test directories (priority 2) \\n- Source directories (priority 3)\\n- Filter by file extensions and relevance\\n```\\n\\n## D) Technical Implementation Details\\n\\n### WriteFileTool Modification\\n```python\\nclass WriteFileTool:\\n    def __init__(\\n        self, \\n        agent_definition: Optional[\\"AgentDefinition\\"] = None,\\n        agent_id: Optional[str] = None,\\n        agent_name: Optional[str] = None,\\n        request_id: Optional[str] = None\\n    ):\\n        # Store tracking context\\n        self.tracking_context = {\\n            \'agent_id\': agent_id,\\n            \'agent_name\': agent_name or (agent_definition.name if agent_definition else \'unknown\'),\\n            \'request_id\': request_id\\n        }\\n    \\n    def execute(self, file_path: str, content: str):\\n        # ... existing file write logic ...\\n        \\n        # Add tracking after successful write\\n        if self.tracking_context[\'agent_id\'] and self.tracking_context[\'request_id\']:\\n            self._record_file_generation(file_path, content)\\n```\\n\\n### ToolRegistry Context Injection\\n```python\\ndef default(agent_definition, agent_id=None, request_id=None):\\n    registry = ToolRegistry()\\n    \\n    # Pass context to tools that support it\\n    registry.register(WriteFileTool(\\n        agent_definition=agent_definition,\\n        agent_id=agent_id,\\n        agent_name=agent_definition.name if agent_definition else None,\\n        request_id=request_id\\n    ))\\n    \\n    return registry\\n```\\n\\n### ActivityTracker Auto-Increment Integration\\n```python\\ndef record_file_generated(self, agent_id, agent_name, request_id, file_path, ...):\\n    # ... existing record logic ...\\n    \\n    # Auto-increment file count\\n    self.increment_request_counts(request_id, files=1)\\n```\\n\\n## E) Data Flow Architecture\\n\\n### Before (Broken):\\n```\\nAgent Executes \\u2192 WriteFileTool \\u2192 File Created \\u2713\\n                      \\u2193\\n                (No tracking) \\u2717\\n                      \\u2193\\n              ActivityTracker (empty) \\u2717\\n                      \\u2193\\n                 API Returns [] \\u2717\\n                      \\u2193\\n                UI Shows \\"No Activity\\" \\u2717\\n```\\n\\n### After (Fixed):\\n```\\nAgent Executes \\u2192 WriteFileTool \\u2192 File Created \\u2713\\n                      \\u2193              \\u2193\\n                Tracking Context \\u2192 ActivityTracker.record_file_generated() \\u2713\\n                      \\u2193              \\u2193\\n                Auto-increment \\u2192 Request Counters Updated \\u2713\\n                      \\u2193\\n                 API Returns [files...] \\u2713\\n                      \\u2193\\n                UI Shows Real Activity \\u2713\\n```\\n\\n## F) Backward Compatibility Strategy\\n\\n### Design Principles:\\n1. **Optional Parameters** - All tracking parameters have defaults\\n2. **Graceful Degradation** - Tools work without tracking context\\n3. **Error Isolation** - Tracking failures don\'t break tool execution\\n4. **Existing Test Compatibility** - No changes to existing test interfaces\\n\\n### Migration Path:\\n- **Phase 1**: Add optional tracking parameters\\n- **Phase 2**: Update calling code to pass context\\n- **Phase 3**: Monitor and validate tracking works\\n- **Phase 4**: Remove old parameter patterns (future)\\n\\n## G) Risk Mitigation\\n\\n### Import Cycles\\n**Risk**: ActivityTracker import in tools.py creates circular dependency\\n**Mitigation**: Use local imports within methods, lazy loading\\n\\n### Performance Impact\\n**Risk**: Tracking adds overhead to file operations\\n**Mitigation**: Minimal tracking code, efficient data structures\\n\\n### Thread Safety\\n**Risk**: Concurrent access to ActivityTracker\\n**Mitigation**: Leverage existing thread-safe implementation\\n\\n### Error Propagation\\n**Risk**: Tracking errors break tool execution\\n**Mitigation**: Comprehensive try-catch around all tracking calls\\n\\n## H) Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Unit Tests:\\n- WriteFileTool with and without tracking context\\n- ActivityTracker increment methods\\n- ToolRegistry context propagation\\n\\n### Integration Tests:\\n- End-to-end agent execution with tracking\\n- API endpoint data validation\\n- UI display verification\\n\\n### Regression Tests:\\n- All existing tool tests continue passing\\n- Backward compatibility validation\\n\\n## I) Deployment Considerations\\n\\n### Zero-Downtime Deployment:\\n- Changes are additive and backward compatible\\n- No API endpoint modifications required\\n- No database schema changes needed\\n\\n### Rollback Strategy:\\n- Simple code revert restores original behavior\\n- No data migration concerns\\n\\n## J) Success Metrics\\n\\n### Primary:\\n- `/api/activity/files` returns files created by agents\\n- `/api/activity/timeline` shows non-zero counts for active requests\\n\\n### Secondary:\\n- Zero regression in existing functionality\\n- All tests pass\\n- Performance overhead < 5%\\n\\n## K) Future Enhancements\\n\\n### Potential Additions:\\n- More granular file type detection\\n- Activity analytics and reporting\\n- Historical activity trending\\n- Performance monitoring integration\\n\\n### Architecture Scalability:\\n- Current design supports future activity types\\n- Extensible tracking context system\\n- Plugin architecture for custom tracking\\n\\n---\\n*Architecture Design: 2026-01-14*\\n*Project: Activity Tracking Fixes*\\n*System Architect: AI Assistant*"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_014wxT8Cn4V68yESUyEscBgU', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/github-bots/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_014wxT8Cn4V68yESUyEscBgU', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# GitHub Sync Bot Requirements\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n- **Milestone**: 2 of 6 in GitHub Bots Suite\\n- **Purpose**: Implement advanced git synchronization capabilities\\n\\n## Core Capabilities\\n1. Remote Synchronization\\n   - Fetch and pull operations from remote repositories\\n   - Support for multiple remote repositories\\n   \\n2. Branch Management\\n   - Rebase operations with robust conflict handling\\n   - Safe stash management (save, restore, list)\\n   \\n3. Error Handling\\n   - Detailed conflict detection\\n   - Clear error reporting\\n   - Preservation of uncommitted changes\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- \\u2713 Successfully rebase branch with upstream changes\\n- \\u2713 Safely stash uncommitted changes before sync\\n- \\u2713 Detect and report conflicts clearly\\n- \\u2713 Restore stashed changes after successful sync\\n- \\u2713 Complete operations within 30 seconds for typical repositories\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Use existing base classes and configuration system\\n- Implement using Test-Driven Development (TDD)\\n- Comprehensive error handling\\n- Logging of all synchronization events\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Full repository migration\\n- Complex merge conflict resolution\\n- Support for non-git version control systems\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Base git configuration and authentication are already set up\\n- Typical repository size is under 1GB\\n- Standard git workflow (single branch, linear history)"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01A4sLp5PSxXVqxaXUP153hz', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Test Strategy - Core Infrastructure & Remote Operations\n\n## Test Overview\n\n**Milestone**: Core Infrastructure & Remote Operations - Establish foundational sync capabilities with remote repository connection management, basic fetch/pull operations, configuration system integration, and core error handling framework\n\n**Test Coverage Goals**:\n- Unit Tests: 85% coverage for business logic\n- Integration Tests: 100% coverage for API endpoints and remote connections\n- End-to-End Tests: Critical sync workflows and error scenarios\n\n## Testing Framework Strategy\n\n**Backend Testing**: pytest with mocks for external dependencies\n**Configuration Testing**: pytest-mock for config system validation\n**Git Operations Testing**: pytest with temporary git repositories\n**Error Handling Testing**: pytest with exception simulation\n**Performance Testing**: pytest-benchmark for 30-second timeout validation\n\n## Test Task Breakdown\n\n### 1. Remote Repository Connection Management Tests\n\n#### Unit Test Tasks\n\n**Task ID**: UT-001\n**Component**: Remote Repository Manager\n**Description**: Test remote repository connection establishment and validation\n**Test Cases**:\n- Valid remote URL connection\n- Invalid remote URL handling\n- Authentication token validation\n- Network timeout scenarios\n- SSL certificate validation\n\n**Task ID**: UT-002\n**Component**: Connection Pool Manager\n**Description**: Test multiple remote repository management\n**Test Cases**:\n- Add/remove remote repositories\n- Connection pooling and reuse\n- Concurrent connection handling\n- Memory leak prevention\n- Connection cleanup on errors\n\n#### Integration Test Tasks\n\n**Task ID**: IT-001\n**Component**: Git Remote Integration\n**Description**: Test actual git remote operations with test repositories\n**Test Cases**:\n- Fetch from remote repository\n- Pull from remote repository\n- Remote branch listing\n- Remote status checking\n- Network failure recovery\n\n### 2. Basic Fetch/Pull Operations Tests\n\n#### Unit Test Tasks\n\n**Task ID**: UT-003\n**Component**: Fetch Operation Handler\n**Description**: Test git fetch operation logic and error handling\n**Test Cases**:\n- Successful fetch with updates\n- Fetch with no updates\n- Fetch with authentication errors\n- Fetch with network interruption\n- Fetch progress tracking\n\n**Task ID**: UT-004\n**Component**: Pull Operation Handler\n**Description**: Test git pull operation logic and merge handling\n**Test Cases**:\n- Fast-forward pull\n- Pull with merge commits\n- Pull with conflicts\n- Pull with uncommitted changes\n- Pull failure recovery\n\n#### Integration Test Tasks\n\n**Task ID**: IT-002\n**Component**: Sync Workflow Integration\n**Description**: Test complete fetch/pull workflows with real git operations\n**Test Cases**:\n- End-to-end fetch and status update\n- End-to-end pull and local merge\n- Stash, pull, unstash workflow\n- Conflict detection and reporting\n- Performance under 30-second constraint\n\n### 3. Configuration System Integration Tests\n\n#### Unit Test Tasks\n\n**Task ID**: UT-005\n**Component**: Configuration Manager\n**Description**: Test configuration loading and validation\n**Test Cases**:\n- Load configuration from files\n- Validate configuration schema\n- Default value handling\n- Invalid configuration rejection\n- Configuration update mechanisms\n\n**Task ID**: UT-006\n**Component**: Git Configuration Integration\n**Description**: Test git-specific configuration management\n**Test Cases**:\n- Git user configuration\n- Remote URL configuration\n- Authentication credential handling\n- Branch configuration\n- Merge strategy configuration\n\n#### Integration Test Tasks\n\n**Task ID**: IT-003\n**Component**: Configuration Persistence\n**Description**: Test configuration storage and retrieval across sessions\n**Test Cases**:\n- Save configuration changes\n- Load configuration on startup\n- Configuration validation on load\n- Migration of old configuration formats\n- Configuration backup and restore\n\n### 4. Core Error Handling Framework Tests\n\n#### Unit Test Tasks\n\n**Task ID**: UT-007\n**Component**: Error Classification System\n**Description**: Test error categorization and handling strategies\n**Test Cases**:\n- Network error classification\n- Git operation error classification\n- Authentication error handling\n- Timeout error handling\n- Unknown error fallback\n\n**Task ID**: UT-008\n**Component**: Error Recovery Manager\n**Description**: Test automatic error recovery mechanisms\n**Test Cases**:\n- Retry logic for transient errors\n- Rollback on operation failures\n- State preservation during errors\n- User notification on errors\n- Error logging and reporting\n\n#### Integration Test Tasks\n\n**Task ID**: IT-004\n**Component**: End-to-End Error Scenarios\n**Description**: Test complete error handling workflows\n**Test Cases**:\n- Network failure during sync\n- Authentication failure recovery\n- Conflict resolution workflow\n- Timeout handling with cleanup\n- Error state recovery on restart\n\n### 5. Stash Management Tests\n\n#### Unit Test Tasks\n\n**Task ID**: UT-009\n**Component**: Stash Operations Manager\n**Description**: Test git stash operations and management\n**Test Cases**:\n- Create stash with uncommitted changes\n- Apply stash after operations\n- List existing stashes\n- Drop unnecessary stashes\n- Stash conflict handling\n\n#### Integration Test Tasks\n\n**Task ID**: IT-005\n**Component**: Safe Sync with Stash\n**Description**: Test complete stash-protected sync operations\n**Test Cases**:\n- Stash, sync, unstash workflow\n- Stash failure handling\n- Partial stash scenarios\n- Stash restoration after errors\n- Multiple stash management\n\n### 6. Performance and Reliability Tests\n\n#### Performance Test Tasks\n\n**Task ID**: PT-001\n**Component**: Sync Operation Performance\n**Description**: Validate 30-second performance constraint\n**Test Cases**:\n- Typical repository sync timing\n- Large repository performance\n- Network latency impact\n- Concurrent operation performance\n- Memory usage during operations\n\n#### Reliability Test Tasks\n\n**Task ID**: RT-001\n**Component**: Long-Running Stability\n**Description**: Test system stability under extended use\n**Test Cases**:\n- Multiple sync cycles\n- Memory leak detection\n- Connection pool stability\n- Error recovery consistency\n- Configuration persistence\n\n### 7. Security and Authentication Tests\n\n#### Security Test Tasks\n\n**Task ID**: ST-001\n**Component**: Credential Management\n**Description**: Test secure handling of authentication credentials\n**Test Cases**:\n- Secure credential storage\n- Credential encryption/decryption\n- Token refresh mechanisms\n- Credential validation\n- Unauthorized access prevention\n\n## Test Data Requirements\n\n### Mock Repositories\n- Small test repository (< 1MB)\n- Medium repository with branches (10-50MB)\n- Repository with merge conflicts\n- Repository with large files\n- Invalid/corrupted repository\n\n### Configuration Test Data\n- Valid configuration templates\n- Invalid configuration samples\n- Migration test configurations\n- Performance test configurations\n- Security test configurations\n\n## Test Environment Setup\n\n### Local Test Environment\n- Git repositories in temp directories\n- Mock HTTP servers for remote simulation\n- Network simulation tools for timeout testing\n- Configuration sandbox environments\n\n### Integration Test Environment\n- Real GitHub test repositories\n- Network failure simulation\n- Authentication test accounts\n- Performance monitoring tools\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n### Coverage Targets\n- **Unit Test Coverage**: 85%+ on business logic components\n- **Integration Coverage**: 100% on public APIs and critical paths\n- **Error Path Coverage**: 95% on error handling scenarios\n\n### Performance Targets\n- All sync operations complete within 30 seconds\n- Memory usage remains stable over 100 operations\n- No connection leaks or resource exhaustion\n\n### Reliability Targets\n- Zero data loss during error scenarios\n- Consistent state recovery after failures\n- 99.9% operation success rate under normal conditions\n\n## Test Execution Priority\n\n### Phase 1: Core Unit Tests\n- UT-001 through UT-009 (Remote, Fetch/Pull, Config, Error, Stash)\n\n### Phase 2: Integration Tests\n- IT-001 through IT-005 (Git Integration, Sync Workflows, Config Persistence, Error Scenarios, Safe Sync)\n\n### Phase 3: Performance & Reliability\n- PT-001, RT-001, ST-001 (Performance, Reliability, Security)\n\n## Testing Dependencies\n\n### External Dependencies to Mock\n- GitHub API endpoints\n- Network connections\n- File system operations\n- Git command execution\n- Authentication services\n\n### Test Infrastructure Requirements\n- pytest framework with fixtures\n- pytest-mock for mocking\n- pytest-benchmark for performance\n- pytest-asyncio for async operations\n- temporary git repositories for integration tests\n\n---\n\n**Total Test Tasks Identified**: 16 tasks\n- Unit Tests: 9 tasks\n- Integration Tests: 5 tasks  \n- Performance Tests: 1 task\n- Reliability Tests: 1 task\n- Security Tests: 1 task\n\n**Estimated Test Implementation Time**: 3-4 sprints\n**Coverage Goal**: 85% unit, 100% integration critical paths'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01A4sLp5PSxXVqxaXUP153hz', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1_20260116_224512.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1_20260116_224512.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Test Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDefines comprehensive test strategy for the project. Identifies unit tests, integration tests, end-to-end tests, and test fixtures needed. Coordinates with Backend Captain and Frontend Captain to ensure all code is thoroughly tested. Breaks testing work into tasks for TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou define what needs to be tested and break testing work into actionable tasks.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create test strategies and task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable testing assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if testing requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\n**Default Testing Strategy** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Unit Test Coverage**: 80%+ for business logic\n**Integration Coverage**: All API endpoints + critical integrations\n**E2E Coverage**: Happy path + critical error scenarios\n**Backend Testing**: pytest or Jest with mocks\n**Frontend Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n**E2E Testing**: Playwright or Cypress for critical flows\n\n**DO NOT ask for clarification about**:\nTesting frameworks (use pytest/Jest)\nCoverage goals (80% unit, 100% integration)\nTest structure (AAA pattern: Arrange, Act, Assert)\nMocking strategy (mock external dependencies)\nCI/CD integration (assume GitHub Actions or similar)\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify code that needs testing:\n  * Backend: API endpoints, business logic, data models\n  * Frontend: Components, user interactions, state changes\n  * Integration: API calls, WebSocket connections, auth flows\n  * E2E: Complete user journeys\n\n**2. Define Test Strategy**\nDetermine test types needed:\n\n**Unit Tests**:\nTest individual functions/methods\nMock external dependencies\nFast, isolated, extensive coverage\n\n**Integration Tests**:\nTest component interactions\nTest API + database integration\nTest frontend + backend communication\n\n**End-to-End Tests**:\nTest complete user flows\nBrowser automation (Playwright, Cypress)\nCritical paths only (expensive to maintain)\n\n**3. Break Down Into Test Tasks**\nFor each component/feature:\nUnit test task (test pure logic)\nIntegration test task (test interactions)\nE2E test task (test user journey) - if critical path\n\n**4. Define Coverage Goals**\nUnit test coverage: 80%+ for business logic\nIntegration coverage: All API endpoints\nE2E coverage: Happy path + critical error cases\n\n**5. Write Test Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Test Strategy - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to test",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write test breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "test_tasks_identified": "integer - number of test tasks created",\n  "coverage_goal": "integer - target code coverage percentage",\n  "task_file": "string - path to test breakdown document",\n  "message": "string - summary of test strategy"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Critical business logic unclear** (can\'t write tests without understanding the logic)\n- **Quality requirements contradictory** (e.g., "100% coverage" + "ship fast")\n- **Security/compliance test requirements unclear** (e.g., specific penetration testing needs)\n- **Performance benchmarks ambiguous** (e.g., "fast" without metrics)\n- **NOT for**: standard testing practices, common coverage goals, typical test frameworks\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Test strategy documented\n- All test tasks identified\n- Coverage goals defined\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for test implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.8\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
