e 1: Performance Benchmarking (Current Model)\n**Objective**: Establish baseline performance metrics for current haiku model\n**Timeline**: 1-2 hours\n**Deliverables**:\n- Current model performance analysis\n- Test execution metrics\n- Success rate documentation\n- Baseline report\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Performance metrics documented for current model\n- Baseline success rate established\n- Test coverage analysis complete\n- Current workflow documented\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n\n### Milestone 2: Model Migration Implementation\n**Objective**: Migrate TDD Coordinator to use sonnet model\n**Timeline**: 2-3 hours\n**Deliverables**:\n- Updated TDD Coordinator configuration\n- Model transition implementation\n- Configuration validation\n- Migration documentation\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- TDD Coordinator successfully using sonnet model\n- All existing functionality preserved\n- Configuration properly updated\n- No breaking changes introduced\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 complete\n\n### Milestone 3: Performance Validation & Comparison\n**Objective**: Validate performance improvements and compare with baseline\n**Timeline**: 2-3 hours\n**Deliverables**:\n- New model performance metrics\n- Comparative analysis report\n- Success rate validation\n- Final recommendation\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Performance improvement of 50% or more achieved\n- No regression in test coverage\n- Comparative analysis documented\n- Validation criteria met\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 2 complete\n\n## Success Criteria\n- Performance improvement of 50% or more\n- No regression in existing test coverage\n- Minimal disruption to current workflow\n- Complete documentation of changes and results\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n- Maintain backup of current configuration\n- Incremental testing approach\n- Rollback plan if performance degrades\n- Documentation of all changes for audit trail'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01HocmHBrnYi5NJmDHLip9JC', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_224247.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_224247.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01GTajbDperHF1np3Td2JBUB', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tdd_coordinator_model_validation_requirements.md', 'project_context': 'TDD Coordinator Model Update - migrating from claude-3-5-haiku-20241022 to claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01GTajbDperHF1np3Td2JBUB', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "architecture_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md", "message": "Comprehensive architecture proposal for TDD Coordinator Model Validation, focusing on systematic performance comparison between Claude models with minimal system disruption", "key_decisions": ["Use Python for model validation framework", "Implement lightweight comparative analysis approach", "Focus on statistically significant performance metrics", "Maintain minimal changes to existing system"], "self_analysis": "The architecture successfully addresses the experimental validation requirements by providing a scientifically rigorous framework for comparing AI models in TDD scenarios. The modular design enables clear separation of concerns while maintaining flexibility for future model comparisons."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_012P3kveman6TgUqAGst3uNN', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_012P3kveman6TgUqAGst3uNN', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# TDD Coordinator Model Validation Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## A) Architecture Overview\\nA focused, lightweight architecture to validate AI model performance improvements with minimal system disruption. The primary goal is to create a comparative validation framework that can systematically measure and compare the performance of two AI models in test-driven development scenarios.\\n\\n## B) Tech Stack\\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\\n- **AI Integration**: Anthropic Claude API\\n- **Performance Tracking**: \\n  - Pandas for data analysis\\n  - Matplotlib/Seaborn for visualization\\n- **Validation Framework**: \\n  - pytest for testing infrastructure\\n  - Custom validation modules\\n\\n### Rationale\\n- Python chosen for its strong data analysis and AI integration capabilities\\n- Lightweight stack to minimize overhead and maintain focus on performance validation\\n- Pandas/Matplotlib provide robust tools for statistical analysis and visualization\\n\\n## C) System Components\\n1. **Model Comparison Manager**\\n   - Manages model switching and performance tracking\\n   - Implements benchmark and comparison logic\\n   - Handles API interactions with Claude models\\n\\n2. **Performance Metrics Collector**\\n   - Captures detailed performance metrics\\n   - Tracks success rates, generation times, test coverage\\n   - Generates comparative reports\\n\\n3. **Validation Executor**\\n   - Runs systematic performance tests\\n   - Applies consistent test scenarios across both models\\n   - Ensures statistically significant sample size\\n\\n## D) File/Directory Structure\\n```\\ntdd_model_validation/\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 model_manager.py        # Model switching and API interaction\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 metrics_collector.py    # Performance tracking\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 validation_executor.py  # Test execution framework\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 utils/                  # Utility modules\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 tests/                      # Validation test cases\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 benchmark_tests.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 comparative_tests.py\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 results/                    # Output metrics and reports\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 raw_metrics/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 reports/\\n\\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 config.yaml                 # Configuration settings\\n```\\n\\n## E) Data Model\\n- Performance Metrics Schema:\\n  ```python\\n  {\\n    \\"model_name\\": str,\\n    \\"test_scenario\\": str,\\n    \\"success_rate\\": float,\\n    \\"generation_time\\": float,\\n    \\"coverage_percentage\\": float\\n  }\\n  ```\\n\\n## F) Validation Strategy\\n1. **Benchmark Current Model**\\n   - Run comprehensive test suite with current model\\n   - Capture baseline metrics\\n   - Establish statistical baseline\\n\\n2. **Model Migration**\\n   - Implement minimal changes to switch between models\\n   - Ensure identical test scenarios and environments\\n\\n3. **Comparative Analysis**\\n   - Run identical test scenarios on new model\\n   - Compare performance metrics\\n   - Statistical significance testing\\n\\n## G) Deployment Considerations\\n- Local execution for initial validation\\n- Containerization with Docker for consistent environment\\n- Potential future CI/CD integration for automated comparisons\\n\\n## H) Risks and Mitigations\\n1. **Risk**: Inconsistent test scenarios\\n   - **Mitigation**: Strict test scenario standardization\\n   - **Approach**: Create reproducible, deterministic test cases\\n\\n2. **Risk**: API rate limits or inconsistencies\\n   - **Mitigation**: Implement robust error handling\\n   - **Approach**: Exponential backoff, comprehensive logging\\n\\n## I) Open Questions\\n- Exact number of test scenarios needed for statistical significance\\n- Specific performance improvement metrics beyond success rate\\n\\n## J) Alternatives Considered\\n- Full system rewrite (Rejected - out of scope)\\n- More complex multi-model comparison framework (Rejected - over-engineering)\\n\\n## K) Success Criteria\\n- 50% performance improvement verification\\n- Minimal system disruption\\n- Reproducible, statistically significant results"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01A7CcdynTfPXiG3DdKDn6WH', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/backend_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Performance Benchmarking - Establish baseline performance metrics for current haiku model', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tdd_coordinator_model_validation_requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01A7CcdynTfPXiG3DdKDn6WH', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "tasks_identified": 9, "task_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md", "dependencies": ["Task 1 \\u2192 Task 2 \\u2192 Task 3 \\u2192 Task 7", "Task 1 \\u2192 Task 9", "Task 2 \\u2192 Task 4 \\u2192 Task 6", "Task 2 \\u2192 Task 4 \\u2192 Task 7", "Task 4 \\u2192 Task 8", "Task 5 (independent)"], "message": "Successfully analyzed performance benchmarking milestone and created 9 backend tasks organized in 4 priority phases. Tasks cover performance metrics collection, database design, benchmark execution services, analytics APIs, and model comparison framework. Critical path identified for establishing haiku model baseline metrics before sonnet model integration. All tasks include specific acceptance criteria and complexity estimates for TDD Coordinator implementation."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01D966yDTSgKmw7XHN98LVe7', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/test_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Performance Benchmarking - Establish baseline performance metrics for current haiku model', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tdd_coordinator_model_validation_requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01D966yDTSgKmw7XHN98LVe7', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "test_tasks_identified": 26, "coverage_goal": 80, "task_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md", "message": "Test strategy created for Performance Benchmarking Milestone 1. Identified 26 test cases across 9 task groups: 3 unit test tasks (metrics collection, statistical analysis, configuration), 3 integration test tasks (model responses, data persistence, activity tracker), 2 E2E test tasks (full execution flow, CLI/API interface), and 1 performance test task. Tests are prioritized in 4 phases with Phase 1 (foundation) being critical path. Mocking strategy defined for Anthropic API, file system, and ActivityTracker. Baseline metrics table prepared for capturing haiku model performance data for comparison in Milestone 2."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XWoeRDddR62wdQTv7hArdw', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/tdd_coordinator', 'input_data': {'problem_description': 'Milestone 1: Performance Benchmarking - Establish baseline performance metrics for current haiku model. Create a validation framework to benchmark the current claude-3-5-haiku-20241022 model performance, including metrics collection, test execution, and baseline reporting for comparison with the target claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929 model.', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/tdd_model_validation', 'test_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/tdd_model_validation/tests', 'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tdd_coordinator_model_validation_requirements.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01XWoeRDddR62wdQTv7hArdw', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": null}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 79.8%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.8\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError, CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError, CircuitBreakerOpenError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I successfully executed the complete Development Manager workflow for this simple but well-structured project. I effectively managed the sequential process: milestone planning, architecture coordinati...\n- I effectively executed the complete planning and implementation workflow for Milestone 1. Successfully coordinated with System Architect for architecture design, spawned all three Coordinators for com...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'require