F1: Backend Log Streaming\\n- **F1.1**: Create WebSocket endpoint `/ws/logs` for real-time log streaming\\n- **F1.2**: Implement log buffer with 1000-entry limit for memory safety\\n- **F1.3**: Structure log entries with timestamp, level, agent_id, request_id, message\\n- **F1.4**: Support server-side filtering by log level (INFO, WARNING, ERROR, DEBUG)\\n- **F1.5**: Support server-side filtering by agent_id and request_id\\n- **F1.6**: Maintain existing logging functionality without performance degradation\\n\\n### F2: Frontend Log Viewer\\n- **F2.1**: Create LogStreamPanel component with WebSocket connection\\n- **F2.2**: Implement auto-scroll with toggle functionality\\n- **F2.3**: Provide log level filter buttons (INFO, WARNING, ERROR, DEBUG)\\n- **F2.4**: Include search filter for agent_id/request_id\\n- **F2.5**: Support pause/resume streaming controls\\n- **F2.6**: Provide clear logs functionality\\n- **F2.7**: Implement color coding by log level\\n- **F2.8**: Display timestamps with relative/absolute toggle\\n\\n### F3: Agent Definition Explorer\\n- **F3.1**: Create AgentExplorer component with tree-view structure\\n- **F3.2**: Display directories: leadership/, coordinators/, developers/, testers/, designers/\\n- **F3.3**: Support collapsible/expandable directories\\n- **F3.4**: Enable file selection with visual feedback\\n- **F3.5**: Use existing `/api/agents` endpoint for data\\n- **F3.6**: Differentiate files and folders with appropriate icons\\n\\n### F4: Agent Definition Editor\\n- **F4.1**: Create AgentDefinitionViewer component with read-only default view\\n- **F4.2**: Implement edit mode toggle with textarea editing\\n- **F4.3**: Provide markdown preview panel\\n- **F4.4**: Integrate with existing `/api/agents/update` endpoint for saving\\n- **F4.5**: Implement automatic backup functionality\\n- **F4.6**: Provide revert functionality using backups\\n- **F4.7**: Display success/error feedback for save operations\\n\\n### F5: Tab Integration\\n- **F5.1**: Add tab navigation to App.jsx with \\"Main View\\" and \\"Logs & Agents\\" tabs\\n- **F5.2**: Preserve all existing functionality in \\"Main View\\" tab\\n- **F5.3**: Implement split-pane layout in \\"Logs & Agents\\" tab\\n- **F5.4**: Ensure responsive design across screen sizes\\n- **F5.5**: Maintain consistent dark theme styling\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### NF1: Performance\\n- Log streaming must not degrade backend performance\\n- WebSocket connections should be efficiently managed\\n- Log buffer must not exceed memory constraints (1000 entries)\\n\\n### NF2: Usability\\n- UI must follow existing design patterns and dark theme\\n- Components must be responsive across different screen sizes\\n- Interface should be intuitive for developers and administrators\\n\\n### NF3: Reliability\\n- WebSocket connections should handle disconnections gracefully\\n- File editing should include backup/recovery mechanisms\\n- Error states should be clearly communicated to users\\n\\n### NF4: Maintainability\\n- Code should follow existing project conventions\\n- Components should be modular and reusable\\n- TDD methodology must be followed (tests before implementation)\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Must use existing WebSocket infrastructure (building on `/ws/agent-status`)\\n- Must use React Bootstrap for UI consistency\\n- Must integrate with existing API endpoints (`/api/agents`, `/api/agents/{tier}/{name}`, `/api/agents/update`)\\n- Must use simple textarea for editing (no Monaco editor requirement)\\n- Must use CSS flexbox for split-pane layout\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. Users can view real-time backend logs without page refresh\\n2. Log streaming includes filtering by level and search terms\\n3. Users can browse agent definition files in intuitive tree structure\\n4. Users can view and edit agent definitions with automatic backup\\n5. Tab integration preserves existing functionality\\n6. System performance remains stable under normal log volume\\n7. All tests pass (following TDD methodology)\\n8. UI maintains consistency with existing design\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Advanced log analysis or aggregation features\\n- Complex code editing features (syntax highlighting, IntelliSense)\\n- User authentication/authorization for file editing\\n- Log persistence to database\\n- Advanced layout customization options\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- Existing WebSocket infrastructure (`/ws/agent-status`)\\n- Existing agent API endpoints\\n- React Bootstrap framework\\n- Current dark theme CSS\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n- Standard log volumes won\'t exceed buffer capacity under normal operation\\n- Users have appropriate permissions for file system access\\n- Existing API endpoints provide sufficient data for agent management\\n- WebSocket infrastructure can handle additional concurrent connections\\n- Current UI framework (React Bootstrap) is sufficient for new components\\n\\n## Testing Requirements\\nFollowing TDD methodology:\\n1. Unit tests for all React components\\n2. Integration tests for WebSocket connections\\n3. API integration tests for agent management\\n4. End-to-end tests for complete user workflows\\n5. Performance tests for log streaming under load"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01LJsQXBLduVYqPimeDBvVEk', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Logs Agents Tab Implementation', 'description': 'Implement Logs & Agents Tab with real-time log streaming and agent file management'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01LJsQXBLduVYqPimeDBvVEk', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "23ed529f", "message": "Created project: Logs Agents Tab Implementation", "summary": {"project_id": "23ed529f", "project_name": "Logs Agents Tab Implementation", "description": "Implement Logs & Agents Tab with real-time log streaming and agent file management", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T2